rmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":null,\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_selection\",\"explanation\":\"There isn\'t just one correct answer.\\nThis situation contains multiple thinking traps.\\nMany people begin with Fortune Telling.\\nOthers immediately move to Catastrophizing.\\nSome begin looking only for information that supports their fears (Confirmation Bias).\\nThe important skill is recognising that your thinking—not the situation—is driving your conclusion.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"tip\":\"Rumours are not evidence. Wait for facts before reaching conclusions.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you actually know?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. Which parts of your thinking are assumptions?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least 3 other explanations that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":3},{\"field_key\":\"one_more_explanation\",\"prompt\":\"Can you think of one explanation that you hadn\'t considered at first?\"}],\"reference_example\":[\"The restructuring may affect reporting lines rather than jobs.\",\"The meeting may involve expansion rather than downsizing.\",\"HR may be preparing managers before communicating changes.\",\"The rumours may be incomplete or inaccurate.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action.\\nThere is usually one reasonable action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available, what is one thoughtful action you can take?\"}],\"reference_example\":\"Continue performing your responsibilities professionally.\\nAttend the organizational meeting with an open mind.\\nWait for official communication before making decisions or reacting to rumours.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete this sentence: \\\"Today I learned that...\\\"\"}],\"reference_example\":\"When uncertainty increases, good judgment becomes even more important. My first thought isn\'t always my best thought.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Which part of today\'s situation was fact, and which part came from your own interpretation?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional journal entry — user may type or speak a personal reflection here (not scored).\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (20, 1, 'The Unexpected Email', 'Workplace', 'Not revealed upfront — independent checkpoint', '', '{\"day\":20,\"phase\":1,\"title\":\"The Unexpected Email\",\"domain\":\"Workplace\",\"mission\":\"Trust the process you\'ve been practising.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Apply the complete ThinkClear Framework independently.\",\"difficulty\":\"Checkpoint (Advanced)\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"Moderate\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"5-6\",\"primary_skill\":\"Internalize (Independent Application)\",\"primary_trap\":\"Not revealed upfront — independent checkpoint\",\"secondary_trap\":null,\"scenario_text\":\"You receive an email from your manager with the subject line:\\n\\\"Please see me before you leave today.\\\"\\nThe email contains no additional details.\\nDuring the day, you notice your manager is busy in meetings and doesn\'t speak to you.\\nA colleague casually asks,\\n\\\"Did you also get that email?\\\"\\nBy lunchtime, you begin wondering whether something is wrong.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"insight\":null,\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"reference_example\":null},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) do you think might be influencing your thinking?\",\"input_type\":\"multi_choice\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Heavy reliance on immediate external acknowledgment.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a course of action because of past investment rather than future value.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":null,\"explanation_reveal\":\"end_of_day\",\"explanation\":\"(No explanation shown — revealed only in end-of-day walkthrough)\",\"note\":\"(More than one may apply)\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"tip\":null,\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports those assumptions?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges them?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What important information is still missing?\"}]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least 4 other explanations that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"reference_example\":null},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"reminder\":null,\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available, what is the most reasonable action?\"}],\"reference_example\":null},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete this sentence: \\\"Today I learned that...\\\"\"}],\"reference_example\":null}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Congratulations. Twenty days ago, ThinkClear guided you through every step. Today, you completed the framework largely on your own. The goal was never to memorize six steps — it was to practise using them until they became familiar. This is the end of Phase 1. Tomorrow, the situations become less structured, the guidance becomes lighter, and the uncertainty becomes greater — but the framework stays the same. You\'re ready for Phase 2.\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional journal entry — user may type or speak a personal reflection here (not scored).\",\"required\":false}},\"end_of_day_walkthrough\":{\"facts\":[\"My manager asked to see me before I leave today.\",\"The email didn\'t explain why.\",\"My manager has been busy in meetings.\",\"A colleague also received a similar email.\"],\"traps_present\":[\"Fortune Telling\",\"Mind Reading\",\"Catastrophizing\"],\"alternative_explanations\":[\"The manager wants to discuss an upcoming project.\",\"It\'s a routine one-to-one meeting.\",\"The manager needs information before tomorrow.\",\"Several team members are meeting individually today.\",\"The meeting has nothing to do with my performance.\"],\"one_reasonable_action\":[\"Attend the meeting with an open mind.\",\"Avoid drawing conclusions before hearing what your manager has to say.\"]}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE `title` = 'The Unexpected Email', `domain` = 'Workplace', `primary_trap` = 'Not revealed upfront — independent checkpoint', `secondary_trap` = '', `content_bundle` = '{\"day\":20,\"phase\":1,\"title\":\"The Unexpected Email\",\"domain\":\"Workplace\",\"mission\":\"Trust the process you\'ve been practising.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Apply the complete ThinkClear Framework independently.\",\"difficulty\":\"Checkpoint (Advanced)\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"Moderate\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"5-6\",\"primary_skill\":\"Internalize (Independent Application)\",\"primary_trap\":\"Not revealed upfront — independent checkpoint\",\"secondary_trap\":null,\"scenario_text\":\"You receive an email from your manager with the subject line:\\n\\\"Please see me before you leave today.\\\"\\nThe email contains no additional details.\\nDuring the day, you notice your manager is busy in meetings and doesn\'t speak to you.\\nA colleague casually asks,\\n\\\"Did you also get that email?\\\"\\nBy lunchtime, you begin wondering whether something is wrong.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"insight\":null,\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"reference_example\":null},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) do you think might be influencing your thinking?\",\"input_type\":\"multi_choice\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Heavy reliance on immediate external acknowledgment.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a course of action because of past investment rather than future value.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":null,\"explanation_reveal\":\"end_of_day\",\"explanation\":\"(No explanation shown — revealed only in end-of-day walkthrough)\",\"note\":\"(More than one may apply)\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"tip\":null,\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports those assumptions?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges them?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What important information is still missing?\"}]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least 4 other explanations that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"reference_example\":null},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"reminder\":null,\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available, what is the most reasonable action?\"}],\"reference_example\":null},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete this sentence: \\\"Today I learned that...\\\"\"}],\"reference_example\":null}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Congratulations. Twenty days ago, ThinkClear guided you through every step. Today, you completed the framework largely on your own. The goal was never to memorize six steps — it was to practise using them until they became familiar. This is the end of Phase 1. Tomorrow, the situations become less structured, the guidance becomes lighter, and the uncertainty becomes greater — but the framework stays the same. You\'re ready for Phase 2.\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional journal entry — user may type or speak a personal reflection here (not scored).\",\"required\":false}},\"end_of_day_walkthrough\":{\"facts\":[\"My manager asked to see me before I leave today.\",\"The email didn\'t explain why.\",\"My manager has been busy in meetings.\",\"A colleague also received a similar email.\"],\"traps_present\":[\"Fortune Telling\",\"Mind Reading\",\"Catastrophizing\"],\"alternative_explanations\":[\"The manager wants to discuss an upcoming project.\",\"It\'s a routine one-to-one meeting.\",\"The manager needs information before tomorrow.\",\"Several team members are meeting individually today.\",\"The meeting has nothing to do with my performance.\"],\"one_reasonable_action\":[\"Attend the meeting with an open mind.\",\"Avoid drawing conclusions before hearing what your manager has to say.\"]}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (21, 2, 'Passed Over for Promotion', 'Business', 'Validation Seeking', 'Mind Reading, Rumination, Confirmation Bias', '{\"day\":21,\"phase\":2,\"title\":\"Passed Over for Promotion\",\"domain\":\"Business\",\"mission\":\"The first explanation isn\'t always the best explanation.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Separate Facts from Stories\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"Moderate\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"4-6\",\"primary_skill\":\"Detect\",\"primary_trap\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Mind Reading, Rumination, Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Mind Reading\",\"Rumination\",\"Confirmation Bias\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate guidance; user is still explicitly prompted through each step.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You\'ve worked in your organization for three years.\\nOver the past year, you\'ve consistently received positive feedback.\\nYour manager has appreciated your work during team meetings.\\nThis month, another colleague is promoted.\\nYou are not.\\nNo explanation is given.\\nDuring lunch, one colleague quietly says, “I thought it would be you.”\\nThe rest of the day, you replay recent conversations with your manager and wonder what you may have done wrong.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts. Then write the story your mind is creating.\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. The story explains what the mind thinks the facts mean.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story/assumptions your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"You have worked in the organization for three years.\",\"You\'ve received positive feedback.\",\"Another colleague was promoted.\",\"You were not.\",\"No explanation has been provided.\"],\"story\":\"My manager no longer believes in me.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: You have worked in the organization for three years. You\'ve received positive feedback. Another colleague was promoted. You were not. No explanation has been provided.\\nStory: My manager no longer believes in me.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"primary_trap\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Mind Reading\",\"Rumination\",\"Confirmation Bias\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"mind_reading\",\"rumination\",\"confirmation_bias\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"The promotion has become a measure of personal worth rather than one organizational decision. Mind Reading, Rumination and Confirmation Bias may also be present.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What facts do you know for certain?\\n• What assumptions are you making?\\n• What evidence supports your conclusion?\\n• What evidence challenges it?\\n• What information is still missing?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"I know I wasn\'t promoted.\",\"I don\'t know why.\",\"Positive feedback suggests my performance has been valued.\",\"I don\'t know what criteria were used.\",\"I haven\'t spoken with my manager yet.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"I know I wasn\'t promoted.\",\"I don\'t know why.\",\"Positive feedback suggests my performance has been valued.\",\"I don\'t know what criteria were used.\",\"I haven\'t spoken with my manager yet.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The promoted colleague had skills needed for that role.\",\"Another opportunity may be planned.\",\"Budget or organizational timing influenced the decision.\",\"The process considered factors you don\'t yet know.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The promoted colleague had skills needed for that role.\",\"Another opportunity may be planned.\",\"Budget or organizational timing influenced the decision.\",\"The process considered factors you don\'t yet know.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Schedule a conversation with your manager.\",\"Ask for specific feedback.\",\"Understand what skills or experience would strengthen future opportunities.\",\"Do not make a career decision based only on an assumption.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Schedule a conversation with your manager.\\nAsk for specific feedback.\\nUnderstand what skills or experience would strengthen future opportunities.\\nDo not make a career decision based only on an assumption.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Not receiving what I expected doesn\'t automatically explain why. Good judgment begins when I separate facts from the story my mind creates.\",\"reference_example\":\"Not receiving what I expected doesn\'t automatically explain why. Good judgment begins when I separate facts from the story my mind creates.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Where else today did I create a story before I had enough evidence?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE `title` = 'Passed Over for Promotion', `domain` = 'Business', `primary_trap` = 'Validation Seeking', `secondary_trap` = 'Mind Reading, Rumination, Confirmation Bias', `content_bundle` = '{\"day\":21,\"phase\":2,\"title\":\"Passed Over for Promotion\",\"domain\":\"Business\",\"mission\":\"The first explanation isn\'t always the best explanation.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Separate Facts from Stories\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"Moderate\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"4-6\",\"primary_skill\":\"Detect\",\"primary_trap\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Mind Reading, Rumination, Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Mind Reading\",\"Rumination\",\"Confirmation Bias\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate guidance; user is still explicitly prompted through each step.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You\'ve worked in your organization for three years.\\nOver the past year, you\'ve consistently received positive feedback.\\nYour manager has appreciated your work during team meetings.\\nThis month, another colleague is promoted.\\nYou are not.\\nNo explanation is given.\\nDuring lunch, one colleague quietly says, “I thought it would be you.”\\nThe rest of the day, you replay recent conversations with your manager and wonder what you may have done wrong.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts. Then write the story your mind is creating.\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. The story explains what the mind thinks the facts mean.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story/assumptions your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"You have worked in the organization for three years.\",\"You\'ve received positive feedback.\",\"Another colleague was promoted.\",\"You were not.\",\"No explanation has been provided.\"],\"story\":\"My manager no longer believes in me.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: You have worked in the organization for three years. You\'ve received positive feedback. Another colleague was promoted. You were not. No explanation has been provided.\\nStory: My manager no longer believes in me.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"primary_trap\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Mind Reading\",\"Rumination\",\"Confirmation Bias\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"mind_reading\",\"rumination\",\"confirmation_bias\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"The promotion has become a measure of personal worth rather than one organizational decision. Mind Reading, Rumination and Confirmation Bias may also be present.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What facts do you know for certain?\\n• What assumptions are you making?\\n• What evidence supports your conclusion?\\n• What evidence challenges it?\\n• What information is still missing?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"I know I wasn\'t promoted.\",\"I don\'t know why.\",\"Positive feedback suggests my performance has been valued.\",\"I don\'t know what criteria were used.\",\"I haven\'t spoken with my manager yet.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"I know I wasn\'t promoted.\",\"I don\'t know why.\",\"Positive feedback suggests my performance has been valued.\",\"I don\'t know what criteria were used.\",\"I haven\'t spoken with my manager yet.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The promoted colleague had skills needed for that role.\",\"Another opportunity may be planned.\",\"Budget or organizational timing influenced the decision.\",\"The process considered factors you don\'t yet know.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The promoted colleague had skills needed for that role.\",\"Another opportunity may be planned.\",\"Budget or organizational timing influenced the decision.\",\"The process considered factors you don\'t yet know.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Schedule a conversation with your manager.\",\"Ask for specific feedback.\",\"Understand what skills or experience would strengthen future opportunities.\",\"Do not make a career decision based only on an assumption.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Schedule a conversation with your manager.\\nAsk for specific feedback.\\nUnderstand what skills or experience would strengthen future opportunities.\\nDo not make a career decision based only on an assumption.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Not receiving what I expected doesn\'t automatically explain why. Good judgment begins when I separate facts from the story my mind creates.\",\"reference_example\":\"Not receiving what I expected doesn\'t automatically explain why. Good judgment begins when I separate facts from the story my mind creates.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Where else today did I create a story before I had enough evidence?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (22, 2, 'The Silent Client', 'Business', 'Mind Reading', 'Fortune Telling, Confirmation Bias', '{\"day\":22,\"phase\":2,\"title\":\"The Silent Client\",\"domain\":\"Business\",\"mission\":\"Silence is information—but it is not an explanation.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Separate Facts from Stories\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"Low\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"4-6\",\"primary_skill\":\"Detect\",\"primary_trap\":\"Mind Reading\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Fortune Telling, Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Fortune Telling\",\"Confirmation Bias\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate guidance; user is still explicitly prompted through each step.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You sent a proposal to an important client.\\nThey usually respond within one or two days.\\nFour days have passed.\\nThey have viewed your message but have not replied.\\nYou have another prospect who is waiting for your attention.\\nYou start thinking the client disliked your proposal and may already be working with someone else.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts. Then write the story your mind is creating.\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. The story explains what the mind thinks the facts mean.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story/assumptions your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"The proposal was sent.\",\"The client usually replies within one or two days.\",\"Four days have passed without a reply.\",\"The message was viewed.\"],\"story\":\"They don\'t want to work with me and are avoiding telling me.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: The proposal was sent. The client usually replies within one or two days. Four days have passed without a reply. The message was viewed.\\nStory: They don\'t want to work with me and are avoiding telling me.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"mind_reading\",\"primary_trap\":\"Mind Reading\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Fortune Telling\",\"Confirmation Bias\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"fortune_telling\",\"confirmation_bias\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Mind Reading is strongest because the client\'s intention is being inferred without evidence. Fortune Telling and Confirmation Bias can amplify the conclusion.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What facts do you know for certain?\\n• What assumptions are you making?\\n• What evidence supports your conclusion?\\n• What evidence challenges it?\\n• What information is still missing?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"There is no reply yet.\",\"I do not know why they have not replied.\",\"The usual response time has passed, but that does not establish the reason.\",\"I do not know whether another decision-maker is involved.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"There is no reply yet.\",\"I do not know why they have not replied.\",\"The usual response time has passed, but that does not establish the reason.\",\"I do not know whether another decision-maker is involved.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"They are reviewing it internally.\",\"A decision-maker is unavailable.\",\"The proposal requires budget approval.\",\"Their priorities changed temporarily.\",\"They may still intend to respond.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"They are reviewing it internally.\",\"A decision-maker is unavailable.\",\"The proposal requires budget approval.\",\"Their priorities changed temporarily.\",\"They may still intend to respond.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Send one concise follow-up.\",\"Set a reasonable follow-up point rather than checking repeatedly.\",\"Continue progressing other opportunities instead of treating this client as either won or lost.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Send one concise follow-up.\\nSet a reasonable follow-up point rather than checking repeatedly.\\nContinue progressing other opportunities instead of treating this client as either won or lost.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"I can respond to what I know without inventing the part I don\'t know.\",\"reference_example\":\"I can respond to what I know without inventing the part I don\'t know.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"When someone is silent, how quickly do you decide what their silence means?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
