l_or_nothing\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Emotional Reasoning turns embarrassment into evidence. Validation Seeking makes feedback feel like a judgment of worth. All-or-Nothing Thinking can convert one area for improvement into total failure.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What facts do you know for certain?\\n• What assumptions are you making?\\n• What evidence supports your conclusion?\\n• What evidence challenges it?\\n• What information is still missing?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"I received both positive and corrective feedback.\",\"I do not know how serious the gaps are until I clarify them.\",\"Feeling embarrassed does not establish poor performance.\",\"The manager did not say I am failing.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"I received both positive and corrective feedback.\",\"I do not know how serious the gaps are until I clarify them.\",\"Feeling embarrassed does not establish poor performance.\",\"The manager did not say I am failing.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The manager expects growth at my level.\",\"The gaps may be specific and fixable.\",\"The feedback may be preparation for greater responsibility.\",\"The manager may be giving useful information early.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The manager expects growth at my level.\",\"The gaps may be specific and fixable.\",\"The feedback may be preparation for greater responsibility.\",\"The manager may be giving useful information early.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Ask for two or three specific examples.\",\"Agree on what improvement would look like.\",\"Review progress after an agreed period.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Ask for two or three specific examples.\\nAgree on what improvement would look like.\\nReview progress after an agreed period.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Feedback about one part of my performance is information—not a verdict on my entire capability.\",\"reference_example\":\"Feedback about one part of my performance is information—not a verdict on my entire capability.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"When feedback hurts, do you evaluate the evidence or the feeling first?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (25, 2, 'The Changed Terms', 'Business', 'Confirmation Bias', 'Sunk Cost Fallacy, Fortune Telling', '{\"day\":25,\"phase\":2,\"title\":\"The Changed Terms\",\"domain\":\"Business\",\"mission\":\"A changing situation requires a fresh judgment.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Generate Alternative Explanations\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"Moderate\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"4-6\",\"primary_skill\":\"Reframe\",\"primary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy, Fortune Telling\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"Fortune Telling\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate guidance; user is still explicitly prompted through each step.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You have spent four months negotiating a large business deal.\\nThe client suddenly changes a major requirement.\\nYour team has already invested significant time preparing the proposal.\\nYou believe the deal will eventually close if you keep pushing.\\nA colleague points out that the new requirement may make the economics unattractive.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts. Then write the story your mind is creating.\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. The story explains what the mind thinks the facts mean.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story/assumptions your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"Four months have been invested.\",\"The client changed a major requirement.\",\"The team has invested substantial time.\",\"The economics may have changed.\",\"The deal has not yet been signed.\"],\"story\":\"We have come this far, so we need to keep going. It will probably work out.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: Four months have been invested. The client changed a major requirement. The team has invested substantial time. The economics may have changed. The deal has not yet been signed.\\nStory: We have come this far, so we need to keep going. It will probably work out.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"primary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"Fortune Telling\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"fortune_telling\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Confirmation Bias may cause you to focus on evidence supporting the deal. Sunk Cost makes past effort feel like a reason to continue. Fortune Telling predicts a successful outcome without sufficient evidence.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What facts do you know for certain?\\n• What assumptions are you making?\\n• What evidence supports your conclusion?\\n• What evidence challenges it?\\n• What information is still missing?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Past effort cannot be recovered.\",\"The commercial terms have changed.\",\"The deal is not yet committed.\",\"The new economics need to be evaluated from today\'s position.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Past effort cannot be recovered.\",\"The commercial terms have changed.\",\"The deal is not yet committed.\",\"The new economics need to be evaluated from today\'s position.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The revised deal may still be profitable.\",\"The client may accept a different structure.\",\"The deal may need to be renegotiated.\",\"Walking away may preserve resources for better opportunities.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The revised deal may still be profitable.\",\"The client may accept a different structure.\",\"The deal may need to be renegotiated.\",\"Walking away may preserve resources for better opportunities.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Recalculate the economics using the new terms.\",\"Compare the revised deal with realistic alternatives.\",\"Continue only if the future value justifies the remaining effort.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Recalculate the economics using the new terms.\\nCompare the revised deal with realistic alternatives.\\nContinue only if the future value justifies the remaining effort.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"A decision should be based on what the opportunity is worth now—not on how much I have already invested.\",\"reference_example\":\"A decision should be based on what the opportunity is worth now—not on how much I have already invested.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Where might you be defending a past decision instead of reassessing the future?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
