er opportunity available.\"],\"story\":\"They finally recognize my value, so staying must be the right decision.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: You had decided to leave before the counteroffer. Your employer has offered more money and a new title. You had concerns about growth before the offer. Some future changes have been promised. You have another opportunity available.\\nStory: They finally recognize my value, so staying must be the right decision.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"primary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Validation Seeking\",\"Confirmation Bias\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"validation_seeking\",\"confirmation_bias\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Sunk Cost can pull you back into the familiar path simply because of your history. Validation Seeking may make the recognition feel like proof that the organization has changed. Confirmation Bias can selectively favor whichever option feels emotionally satisfying.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What facts do you know for certain?\\n• What assumptions are you making?\\n• What evidence supports your conclusion?\\n• What evidence challenges it?\\n• What information is still missing?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The salary has changed.\",\"The title has changed.\",\"I need to verify what will actually change in role, authority and growth.\",\"The original problems may or may not be resolved.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The salary has changed.\",\"The title has changed.\",\"I need to verify what will actually change in role, authority and growth.\",\"The original problems may or may not be resolved.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate at least four plausible alternatives. At least one should challenge your first interpretation.\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The counteroffer may genuinely solve the problem.\",\"The counteroffer may address compensation but not development.\",\"The external opportunity may offer a different learning path.\",\"I may be able to negotiate specific conditions before deciding.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The counteroffer may genuinely solve the problem.\",\"The counteroffer may address compensation but not development.\",\"The external opportunity may offer a different learning path.\",\"I may be able to negotiate specific conditions before deciding.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"Choose one reasonable next action. Explain what it will help you learn, clarify or protect.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Compare both roles on the factors that originally led to the resignation.\",\"Get important promises documented where appropriate.\",\"Decide based on future fit rather than the emotional effect of being retained.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Compare both roles on the factors that originally led to the resignation.\\nGet important promises documented where appropriate.\\nDecide based on future fit rather than the emotional effect of being retained.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Feeling valued is meaningful, but I still need to evaluate whether the underlying conditions have changed.\",\"reference_example\":\"Feeling valued is meaningful, but I still need to evaluate whether the underlying conditions have changed.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"If the counteroffer had no salary increase, what would you think about the underlying job?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (27, 2, 'The Difficult High Performer', 'Leadership', 'All-or-Nothing Thinking', 'Emotional Reasoning, Validation Seeking', '{\"day\":27,\"phase\":2,\"title\":\"The Difficult High Performer\",\"domain\":\"Leadership\",\"mission\":\"Strong results do not automatically cancel out damaging behaviour.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Generate Alternative Explanations\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"Moderate\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"4-6\",\"primary_skill\":\"Reframe\",\"primary_trap\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning, Validation Seeking\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"Validation Seeking\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate-to-reduced guidance; user must defend the next action and work with competing information.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Defend → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"One of your strongest employees consistently exceeds targets.\\nHowever, several team members report that the person is dismissive and difficult to work with.\\nYou have personally seen two tense interactions.\\nThe employee argues that high performers are held to a different standard.\\nYou must decide how to address the situation.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"Before you interpret the situation, identify the facts, then state the story or conclusion your mind is moving toward.\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. The story explains what the mind thinks the facts mean.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story/assumptions your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"The employee delivers strong results.\",\"Multiple colleagues have raised concerns.\",\"You have observed two tense interactions.\",\"The employee disagrees with the feedback.\",\"Team dynamics may be affected.\"],\"story\":\"Either I protect my best performer or I risk losing the business.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: The employee delivers strong results. Multiple colleagues have raised concerns. You have observed two tense interactions. The employee disagrees with the feedback. Team dynamics may be affected.\\nStory: Either I protect my best performer or I risk losing the business.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"primary_trap\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"Validation Seeking\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"emotional_reasoning\",\"validation_seeking\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking creates a false choice between performance and behaviour. Emotional Reasoning may arise from frustration. Validation Seeking may make the leader reluctant to challenge someone whose results validate the team.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What facts do you know for certain?\\n• What assumptions are you making?\\n• What evidence supports your conclusion?\\n• What evidence challenges it?\\n• What information is still missing?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Performance is strong.\",\"Behaviour concerns have been raised repeatedly.\",\"The concerns need specific evidence rather than labels.\",\"The business impact of both performance and behaviour matters.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Performance is strong.\",\"Behaviour concerns have been raised repeatedly.\",\"The concerns need specific evidence rather than labels.\",\"The business impact of both performance and behaviour matters.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate at least four plausible alternatives. At least one should challenge your first interpretation.\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The behaviour is a correctable leadership gap.\",\"The reports may contain misunderstandings that need investigation.\",\"The employee may respond well to clear expectations.\",\"Strong performance and behavioural accountability can coexist.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The behaviour is a correctable leadership gap.\",\"The reports may contain misunderstandings that need investigation.\",\"The employee may respond well to clear expectations.\",\"Strong performance and behavioural accountability can coexist.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"Choose one reasonable next action. Explain what it will help you learn, clarify or protect.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Gather specific examples.\",\"Discuss the behaviour privately and clearly.\",\"Set measurable expectations and a review period.\",\"Assess both results and team impact over time.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Gather specific examples.\\nDiscuss the behaviour privately and clearly.\\nSet measurable expectations and a review period.\\nAssess both results and team impact over time.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Good judgment does not require choosing between two extremes when both performance and behaviour matter.\",\"reference_example\":\"Good judgment does not require choosing between two extremes when both performance and behaviour matter.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Where have you created an either-or choice when two considerations could be handled together?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
