idation Seeking\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"emotional_reasoning\",\"validation_seeking\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking creates a false choice between performance and behaviour. Emotional Reasoning may arise from frustration. Validation Seeking may make the leader reluctant to challenge someone whose results validate the team.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What facts do you know for certain?\\n• What assumptions are you making?\\n• What evidence supports your conclusion?\\n• What evidence challenges it?\\n• What information is still missing?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Performance is strong.\",\"Behaviour concerns have been raised repeatedly.\",\"The concerns need specific evidence rather than labels.\",\"The business impact of both performance and behaviour matters.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Performance is strong.\",\"Behaviour concerns have been raised repeatedly.\",\"The concerns need specific evidence rather than labels.\",\"The business impact of both performance and behaviour matters.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate at least four plausible alternatives. At least one should challenge your first interpretation.\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The behaviour is a correctable leadership gap.\",\"The reports may contain misunderstandings that need investigation.\",\"The employee may respond well to clear expectations.\",\"Strong performance and behavioural accountability can coexist.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The behaviour is a correctable leadership gap.\",\"The reports may contain misunderstandings that need investigation.\",\"The employee may respond well to clear expectations.\",\"Strong performance and behavioural accountability can coexist.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"Choose one reasonable next action. Explain what it will help you learn, clarify or protect.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Gather specific examples.\",\"Discuss the behaviour privately and clearly.\",\"Set measurable expectations and a review period.\",\"Assess both results and team impact over time.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Gather specific examples.\\nDiscuss the behaviour privately and clearly.\\nSet measurable expectations and a review period.\\nAssess both results and team impact over time.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Good judgment does not require choosing between two extremes when both performance and behaviour matter.\",\"reference_example\":\"Good judgment does not require choosing between two extremes when both performance and behaviour matter.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Where have you created an either-or choice when two considerations could be handled together?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (28, 2, 'The Family Business Request', 'Family', 'Validation Seeking', 'Mind Reading, Emotional Reasoning', '{\"day\":28,\"phase\":2,\"title\":\"The Family Business Request\",\"domain\":\"Family\",\"mission\":\"Love and responsibility can coexist with careful judgment.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Test Assumptions with Evidence\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"4-6\",\"primary_skill\":\"Reality Check\",\"primary_trap\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Mind Reading, Emotional Reasoning\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Mind Reading\",\"Emotional Reasoning\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate-to-reduced guidance; user must defend the next action and work with competing information.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Defend → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"A close family member asks you to invest in a new business.\\nThey say they need your support and that the opportunity is excellent.\\nYou trust them personally.\\nThey have not yet shared detailed financial projections.\\nYou worry that asking difficult questions may make them feel that you don\'t believe in them.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"Before you interpret the situation, identify the facts, then state the story or conclusion your mind is moving toward.\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. The story explains what the mind thinks the facts mean.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story/assumptions your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"A family member has requested an investment.\",\"You trust the person personally.\",\"The business opportunity has been described positively.\",\"Detailed financial information has not yet been provided.\",\"You feel pressure to show support.\"],\"story\":\"If I ask too many questions, they will think I don\'t support them.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: A family member has requested an investment. You trust the person personally. The business opportunity has been described positively. Detailed financial information has not yet been provided. You feel pressure to show support.\\nStory: If I ask too many questions, they will think I don\'t support them.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"primary_trap\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Mind Reading\",\"Emotional Reasoning\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"mind_reading\",\"emotional_reasoning\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Validation Seeking can make approval from a loved one influence the financial decision. Mind Reading assumes how they will react. Emotional Reasoning treats discomfort about questioning them as evidence that questioning is wrong.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What facts do you know for certain?\\n• What assumptions are you making?\\n• What evidence supports your conclusion?\\n• What evidence challenges it?\\n• What information is still missing?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The relationship and investment are separate considerations.\",\"I do not yet have enough financial information.\",\"I can support someone without automatically investing.\",\"I do not know how they will respond to reasonable questions.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The relationship and investment are separate considerations.\",\"I do not yet have enough financial information.\",\"I can support someone without automatically investing.\",\"I do not know how they will respond to reasonable questions.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate at least four plausible alternatives. At least one should challenge your first interpretation.\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"They may welcome rigorous questions.\",\"The business may be viable but need better planning.\",\"I may support them in another way.\",\"The investment may be inappropriate even if the relationship is strong.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"They may welcome rigorous questions.\",\"The business may be viable but need better planning.\",\"I may support them in another way.\",\"The investment may be inappropriate even if the relationship is strong.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"Choose one reasonable next action. Explain what it will help you learn, clarify or protect.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Ask for the same information you would require for any significant investment.\",\"Separate the relationship decision from the financial decision.\",\"Do not commit until the material information is available.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Ask for the same information you would require for any significant investment.\\nSeparate the relationship decision from the financial decision.\\nDo not commit until the material information is available.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Supporting someone does not require suspending judgment.\",\"reference_example\":\"Supporting someone does not require suspending judgment.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Where does the desire to avoid disappointing someone influence your decisions?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE `title` = 'The Family Business Request', `domain` = 'Family', `primary_trap` = 'Validation Seeking', `secondary_trap` = 'Mind Reading, Emotional Reasoning', `content_bundle` = '{\"day\":28,\"phase\":2,\"title\":\"The Family Business Request\",\"domain\":\"Family\",\"mission\":\"Love and responsibility can coexist with careful judgment.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Test Assumptions with Evidence\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"4-6\",\"primary_skill\":\"Reality Check\",\"primary_trap\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Mind Reading, Emotional Reasoning\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Mind Reading\",\"Emotional Reasoning\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate-to-reduced guidance; user must defend the next action and work with competing information.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Defend → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"A close family member asks you to invest in a new business.\\nThey say they need your support and that the opportunity is excellent.\\nYou trust them personally.\\nThey have not yet shared detailed financial projections.\\nYou worry that asking difficult questions may make them feel that you don\'t believe in them.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"Before you interpret the situation, identify the facts, then state the story or conclusion your mind is moving toward.\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. The story explains what the mind thinks the facts mean.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story/assumptions your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"A family member has requested an investment.\",\"You trust the person personally.\",\"The business opportunity has been described positively.\",\"Detailed financial information has not yet been provided.\",\"You feel pressure to show support.\"],\"story\":\"If I ask too many questions, they will think I don\'t support them.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: A family member has requested an investment. You trust the person personally. The business opportunity has been described positively. Detailed financial information has not yet been provided. You feel pressure to show support.\\nStory: If I ask too many questions, they will think I don\'t support them.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"primary_trap\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Mind Reading\",\"Emotional Reasoning\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"mind_reading\",\"emotional_reasoning\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Validation Seeking can make approval from a loved one influence the financial decision. Mind Reading assumes how they will react. Emotional Reasoning treats discomfort about questioning them as evidence that questioning is wrong.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What facts do you know for certain?\\n• What assumptions are you making?\\n• What evidence supports your conclusion?\\n• What evidence challenges it?\\n• What information is still missing?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The relationship and investment are separate considerations.\",\"I do not yet have enough financial information.\",\"I can support someone without automatically investing.\",\"I do not know how they will respond to reasonable questions.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The relationship and investment are separate considerations.\",\"I do not yet have enough financial information.\",\"I can support someone without automatically investing.\",\"I do not know how they will respond to reasonable questions.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate at least four plausible alternatives. At least one should challenge your first interpretation.\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"They may welcome rigorous questions.\",\"The business may be viable but need better planning.\",\"I may support them in another way.\",\"The investment may be inappropriate even if the relationship is strong.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"They may welcome rigorous questions.\",\"The business may be viable but need better planning.\",\"I may support them in another way.\",\"The investment may be inappropriate even if the relationship is strong.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"Choose one reasonable next action. Explain what it will help you learn, clarify or protect.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Ask for the same information you would require for any significant investment.\",\"Separate the relationship decision from the financial decision.\",\"Do not commit until the material information is available.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Ask for the same information you would require for any significant investment.\\nSeparate the relationship decision from the financial decision.\\nDo not commit until the material information is available.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Supporting someone does not require suspending judgment.\",\"reference_example\":\"Supporting someone does not require suspending judgment.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Where does the desire to avoid disappointing someone influence your decisions?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (29, 2, 'The Falling Investment', 'Finance', 'Confirmation Bias', 'Fortune Telling, Sunk Cost Fallacy', '{\"day\":29,\"phase\":2,\"title\":\"The Falling Investment\",\"domain\":\"Finance\",\"mission\":\"Confidence is not evidence.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Recognize Thinking Traps\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"Moderate\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"4-6\",\"primary_skill\":\"Decode\",\"primary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Fortune Telling, Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Fortune Telling\",\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate-to-reduced guidance; user must defend the next action and work with competing information.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Defend → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You invested in a company because you believed its growth story was compelling.\\nThe share price has fallen substantially.\\nYou find several online posts explaining why the decline is temporary.\\nYou ignore information that questions the original business thesis.\\nYou are deciding whether to invest more money.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"Before you interpret the situation, identify the facts, then state the story or conclusion your mind is moving toward.\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. The story explains what the mind thinks the facts mean.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story/assumptions your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"The investment has fallen.\",\"You still believe in the original thesis.\",\"Some sources support your view.\",\"Other information challenges it.\",\"You are considering adding more money.\"],\"story\":\"The market is wrong. If I buy more now, the recovery will prove me right.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: The investment has fallen. You still believe in the original thesis. Some sources support your view. Other information challenges it. You are considering adding more money.\\nStory: The market is wrong. If I buy more now, the recovery will prove me right.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"primary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Fortune Telling\",\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"fortune_telling\",\"sunk_cost_fallacy\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Confirmation Bias can make supportive information easier to notice. Sunk Cost can make the existing investment feel like a reason to continue. Fortune Telling can turn an expected recovery into a certainty.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What facts do you know for certain?\\n• What assumptions are you making?\\n• What evidence supports your conclusion?\\n• What evidence challenges it?\\n• What information is still missing?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The price decline is real.\",\"The original thesis may or may not still hold.\",\"Past investment does not justify a new investment by itself.\",\"A future recovery is uncertain.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The price decline is real.\",\"The original thesis may or may not still hold.\",\"Past investment does not justify a new investment by itself.\",\"A future recovery is uncertain.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate at least four plausible alternatives. At least one should challenge your first interpretation.\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The original thesis may still be valid.\",\"The business fundamentals may have changed.\",\"The decline may reflect broader market conditions.\",\"There may be better uses for additional capital.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The original thesis may still be valid.\",\"The business fundamentals may have changed.\",\"The decline may reflect broader market conditions.\",\"There may be better uses for additional capital.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"Choose one reasonable next action. Explain what it will help you learn, clarify or protect.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Reassess the business using current information as if you did not already own it.\",\"Define what evidence would invalidate the original thesis.\",\"Do not add capital solely to reduce the psychological discomfort of a loss.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Reassess the business using current information as if you did not already own it.\\nDefine what evidence would invalidate the original thesis.\\nDo not add capital solely to reduce the psychological discomfort of a loss.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"A new investment deserves a fresh decision, even when I already own the asset.\",\"reference_example\":\"A new investment deserves a fresh decision, even when I already own the asset.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"If you did not own this investment today, would the current evidence make you buy it?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
