"explanation\":\"Mind Reading infers intent from limited behaviour. Emotional Reasoning makes the feeling of being dismissed feel like proof. Confirmation Bias can cause later events to be interpreted as evidence of the same story.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What facts do you know for certain?\\n• What assumptions are you making?\\n• What evidence supports your conclusion?\\n• What evidence challenges it?\\n• What information is still missing?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The proposal was rejected.\",\"The reason is not fully understood.\",\"A separate conversation occurred.\",\"There is no evidence yet that the partner intends to exclude you.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The proposal was rejected.\",\"The reason is not fully understood.\",\"A separate conversation occurred.\",\"There is no evidence yet that the partner intends to exclude you.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate at least four plausible alternatives. At least one should challenge your first interpretation.\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The partner wanted another perspective.\",\"The partner had concerns about the proposal itself.\",\"The discussion may have been operational rather than personal.\",\"There may be a communication problem rather than a trust problem.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The partner wanted another perspective.\",\"The partner had concerns about the proposal itself.\",\"The discussion may have been operational rather than personal.\",\"There may be a communication problem rather than a trust problem.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"Choose one reasonable next action. Explain what it will help you learn, clarify or protect.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Have a direct conversation focused on the decision and roles.\",\"Ask what concerns led to the rejection.\",\"Clarify how major decisions should be discussed between partners.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Have a direct conversation focused on the decision and roles.\\nAsk what concerns led to the rejection.\\nClarify how major decisions should be discussed between partners.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"I can address a relationship problem without first deciding what the other person intended.\",\"reference_example\":\"I can address a relationship problem without first deciding what the other person intended.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"When you feel dismissed, do you ask for clarification or immediately assign an intention?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (31, 2, 'The Urgent Resignation', 'Career', 'Emotional Reasoning', 'Sunk Cost Fallacy, All-or-Nothing Thinking', '{\"day\":31,\"phase\":2,\"title\":\"The Urgent Resignation\",\"domain\":\"Career\",\"mission\":\"A decision becomes clearer when the problem is separated from the impulse.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Make a Decision Using the Complete Framework\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate–Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"5-7\",\"primary_skill\":\"Intervention\",\"primary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy, All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Reduced guidance; decision, trade-offs and opportunity cost are central.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Defend → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You have been unhappy in your current job for the past year.\\nYour workload has increased and your manager has changed twice.\\nYou have a stable income and strong professional relationships.\\nA new opportunity has appeared, but it requires moving to a different city.\\nYou are tempted to resign immediately after a particularly difficult week.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"Start without looking for the \'right\' answer. Write what you know, what you think it means, and what you are tempted to do.\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. The story explains what the mind thinks the facts mean.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story/assumptions your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"You have experienced dissatisfaction for about a year.\",\"Workload has increased.\",\"Management has changed twice.\",\"You have stable income and established relationships.\",\"A new opportunity requires relocation.\",\"The immediate urge to resign is stronger after a difficult week.\"],\"story\":\"I can\'t take this anymore. I need to leave now.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: You have experienced dissatisfaction for about a year. Workload has increased. Management has changed twice. You have stable income and established relationships. A new opportunity requires relocation. The immediate urge to resign is stronger after a difficult week.\\nStory: I can\'t take this anymore. I need to leave now.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"primary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"all_or_nothing\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Emotional Reasoning can turn current frustration into a complete decision. Sunk Cost may pull you toward staying because of what you\'ve built. All-or-Nothing Thinking can make the choice appear to be stay and suffer or leave immediately.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Build your own reality check. Identify the facts, assumptions, evidence for and against your view, and the missing information that could materially change the decision.\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The dissatisfaction predates this week\'s event.\",\"The new opportunity has benefits and costs.\",\"I need more information about the new role and relocation.\",\"Staying also has a cost: opportunity cost, growth and continued dissatisfaction.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The dissatisfaction predates this week\'s event.\",\"The new opportunity has benefits and costs.\",\"I need more information about the new role and relocation.\",\"Staying also has a cost: opportunity cost, growth and continued dissatisfaction.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate the realistic alternatives available to you. Include at least one option that is not your preferred choice and, where relevant, an option that changes the structure of the decision rather than simply choosing A or B.\",\"insight\":\"A decision can improve when you change the question from “Which option wins?” to “What options, conditions or safeguards could make the decision better?”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The new role may be a better fit.\",\"The new role may have hidden problems.\",\"The current role may improve with specific changes.\",\"A transition plan could allow a deliberate move rather than an emotional exit.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The new role may be a better fit.\",\"The new role may have hidden problems.\",\"The current role may improve with specific changes.\",\"A transition plan could allow a deliberate move rather than an emotional exit.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and why? If this is a decision rather than an immediate reaction, state what information, negotiation, experiment or safeguard should come before the final commitment.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Evaluate the new role against the reasons you are unhappy.\",\"Clarify compensation, responsibilities, growth, relocation and risks.\",\"Set a decision date rather than resigning during peak frustration.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Evaluate the new role against the reasons you are unhappy.\\nClarify compensation, responsibilities, growth, relocation and risks.\\nSet a decision date rather than resigning during peak frustration.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “The judgment principle I want to carry forward is…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"A strong feeling can signal that a decision deserves attention; it does not by itself determine the decision.\",\"reference_example\":\"A strong feeling can signal that a decision deserves attention; it does not by itself determine the decision.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Which part of your decision would remain if today\'s emotion were removed?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
