tablished relationships.\",\"A new opportunity requires relocation.\",\"The immediate urge to resign is stronger after a difficult week.\"],\"story\":\"I can\'t take this anymore. I need to leave now.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: You have experienced dissatisfaction for about a year. Workload has increased. Management has changed twice. You have stable income and established relationships. A new opportunity requires relocation. The immediate urge to resign is stronger after a difficult week.\\nStory: I can\'t take this anymore. I need to leave now.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"primary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"all_or_nothing\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Emotional Reasoning can turn current frustration into a complete decision. Sunk Cost may pull you toward staying because of what you\'ve built. All-or-Nothing Thinking can make the choice appear to be stay and suffer or leave immediately.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Build your own reality check. Identify the facts, assumptions, evidence for and against your view, and the missing information that could materially change the decision.\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The dissatisfaction predates this week\'s event.\",\"The new opportunity has benefits and costs.\",\"I need more information about the new role and relocation.\",\"Staying also has a cost: opportunity cost, growth and continued dissatisfaction.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The dissatisfaction predates this week\'s event.\",\"The new opportunity has benefits and costs.\",\"I need more information about the new role and relocation.\",\"Staying also has a cost: opportunity cost, growth and continued dissatisfaction.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate the realistic alternatives available to you. Include at least one option that is not your preferred choice and, where relevant, an option that changes the structure of the decision rather than simply choosing A or B.\",\"insight\":\"A decision can improve when you change the question from “Which option wins?” to “What options, conditions or safeguards could make the decision better?”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The new role may be a better fit.\",\"The new role may have hidden problems.\",\"The current role may improve with specific changes.\",\"A transition plan could allow a deliberate move rather than an emotional exit.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The new role may be a better fit.\",\"The new role may have hidden problems.\",\"The current role may improve with specific changes.\",\"A transition plan could allow a deliberate move rather than an emotional exit.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and why? If this is a decision rather than an immediate reaction, state what information, negotiation, experiment or safeguard should come before the final commitment.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Evaluate the new role against the reasons you are unhappy.\",\"Clarify compensation, responsibilities, growth, relocation and risks.\",\"Set a decision date rather than resigning during peak frustration.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Evaluate the new role against the reasons you are unhappy.\\nClarify compensation, responsibilities, growth, relocation and risks.\\nSet a decision date rather than resigning during peak frustration.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “The judgment principle I want to carry forward is…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"A strong feeling can signal that a decision deserves attention; it does not by itself determine the decision.\",\"reference_example\":\"A strong feeling can signal that a decision deserves attention; it does not by itself determine the decision.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Which part of your decision would remain if today\'s emotion were removed?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (32, 2, 'The Relocation Offer', 'Career', 'Fortune Telling', 'Catastrophizing, Validation Seeking', '{\"day\":32,\"phase\":2,\"title\":\"The Relocation Offer\",\"domain\":\"Career\",\"mission\":\"A bigger opportunity can also contain bigger unknowns.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Test Assumptions with Evidence\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate–Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"5-7\",\"primary_skill\":\"Reality Check\",\"primary_trap\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Catastrophizing, Validation Seeking\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Catastrophizing\",\"Validation Seeking\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Reduced guidance; decision, trade-offs and opportunity cost are central.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Defend → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You receive an offer to relocate to another city for a senior role.\\nThe salary is substantially higher.\\nThe role also involves more responsibility and a longer commute.\\nYour partner is unsure about relocating.\\nYou are excited by the career opportunity but afraid that declining it will permanently limit your growth.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"Start without looking for the \'right\' answer. Write what you know, what you think it means, and what you are tempted to do.\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. The story explains what the mind thinks the facts mean.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story/assumptions your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"The offer is for a senior role.\",\"The salary is higher.\",\"The role has greater responsibility.\",\"The commute is longer.\",\"Your partner is uncertain about relocation.\",\"You do not know whether another similar opportunity will appear.\"],\"story\":\"If I don\'t take this now, I may never get another opportunity like it.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: The offer is for a senior role. The salary is higher. The role has greater responsibility. The commute is longer. Your partner is uncertain about relocation. You do not know whether another similar opportunity will appear.\\nStory: If I don\'t take this now, I may never get another opportunity like it.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"primary_trap\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Catastrophizing\",\"Validation Seeking\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"catastrophizing\",\"validation_seeking\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Fortune Telling treats an uncertain future as certain. Catastrophizing can exaggerate the consequences of declining. Validation Seeking may make the title and salary dominate the evaluation.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Build your own reality check. Identify the facts, assumptions, evidence for and against your view, and the missing information that could materially change the decision.\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"This opportunity exists now.\",\"Future opportunities are unknown.\",\"The decision affects more than career progression.\",\"The practical costs need to be quantified rather than assumed.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"This opportunity exists now.\",\"Future opportunities are unknown.\",\"The decision affects more than career progression.\",\"The practical costs need to be quantified rather than assumed.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate the realistic alternatives available to you. Include at least one option that is not your preferred choice and, where relevant, an option that changes the structure of the decision rather than simply choosing A or B.\",\"insight\":\"A decision can improve when you change the question from “Which option wins?” to “What options, conditions or safeguards could make the decision better?”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The opportunity may materially accelerate growth.\",\"The role may not be sustainable after relocation.\",\"A different structure or relocation support may change the decision.\",\"Another opportunity may arise later, even if timing is uncertain.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The opportunity may materially accelerate growth.\",\"The role may not be sustainable after relocation.\",\"A different structure or relocation support may change the decision.\",\"Another opportunity may arise later, even if timing is uncertain.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and why? If this is a decision rather than an immediate reaction, state what information, negotiation, experiment or safeguard should come before the final commitment.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"List the decision factors and identify which require actual information.\",\"Clarify the role, authority, expected outcomes, relocation support and work pattern.\",\"Discuss the household impact before deciding.\"],\"reference_example\":\"List the decision factors and identify which require actual information.\\nClarify the role, authority, expected outcomes, relocation support and work pattern.\\nDiscuss the household impact before deciding.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “The judgment principle I want to carry forward is…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"I don\'t need certainty about the future to make a good decision; I need clarity about the assumptions driving it.\",\"reference_example\":\"I don\'t need certainty about the future to make a good decision; I need clarity about the assumptions driving it.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Which part of a major opportunity are you treating as inevitable rather than uncertain?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
