al\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Confirmation Bias may cause the team to emphasize strong quarters while overlooking concentration risk. Validation Seeking can make expansion feel like proof of success. Fortune Telling assumes the second location will reproduce the first location\'s performance.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Build your own reality check. Identify the facts, assumptions, evidence for and against your view, and the missing information that could materially change the decision.\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Recent performance is positive.\",\"Revenue concentration creates uncertainty.\",\"The second location has additional costs.\",\"The first location\'s performance does not prove the second location will perform identically.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Recent performance is positive.\",\"Revenue concentration creates uncertainty.\",\"The second location has additional costs.\",\"The first location\'s performance does not prove the second location will perform identically.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate the realistic alternatives available to you. Include at least one option that is not your preferred choice and, where relevant, an option that changes the structure of the decision rather than simply choosing A or B.\",\"insight\":\"A decision can improve when you change the question from “Which option wins?” to “What options, conditions or safeguards could make the decision better?”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Expansion may work if demand is sufficiently diversified.\",\"A smaller pilot could test demand.\",\"Strengthening the first location may create more durable growth.\",\"Expansion may be premature.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Expansion may work if demand is sufficiently diversified.\",\"A smaller pilot could test demand.\",\"Strengthening the first location may create more durable growth.\",\"Expansion may be premature.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and why? If this is a decision rather than an immediate reaction, state what information, negotiation, experiment or safeguard should come before the final commitment.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Stress-test the economics without assuming the large client continues.\",\"Define minimum demand and cash-flow thresholds.\",\"Consider a lower-commitment pilot before full expansion.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Stress-test the economics without assuming the large client continues.\\nDefine minimum demand and cash-flow thresholds.\\nConsider a lower-commitment pilot before full expansion.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “The judgment principle I want to carry forward is…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Past growth is evidence to examine—not permission to stop examining.\",\"reference_example\":\"Past growth is evidence to examine—not permission to stop examining.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"What evidence would make you change your mind about expansion?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (35, 2, 'The Unfinished Degree', 'Career', 'Sunk Cost Fallacy', 'Confirmation Bias, All-or-Nothing Thinking', '{\"day\":35,\"phase\":2,\"title\":\"The Unfinished Degree\",\"domain\":\"Career\",\"mission\":\"The time already spent cannot be recovered; the future still can be chosen.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Make a Decision Using the Complete Framework\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate–Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"Moderate\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"5-7\",\"primary_skill\":\"Internalize\",\"primary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias, All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Confirmation Bias\",\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Reduced guidance; decision, trade-offs and opportunity cost are central.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Defend → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You enrolled in a two-year professional program.\\nYou are halfway through.\\nYour career interests have changed substantially since you enrolled.\\nFinishing would take another year and require weekends and substantial fees.\\nLeaving would free time for a different path, but you worry that stopping means admitting you made a mistake.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"Start without looking for the \'right\' answer. Write what you know, what you think it means, and what you are tempted to do.\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. The story explains what the mind thinks the facts mean.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story/assumptions your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"You are halfway through the program.\",\"You have already invested time and money.\",\"Your career interests have changed.\",\"One year and additional fees remain.\",\"Leaving would create time for another path.\"],\"story\":\"I have already come this far. Leaving would mean the whole decision was a mistake.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: You are halfway through the program. You have already invested time and money. Your career interests have changed. One year and additional fees remain. Leaving would create time for another path.\\nStory: I have already come this far. Leaving would mean the whole decision was a mistake.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"primary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Confirmation Bias\",\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"confirmation_bias\",\"all_or_nothing\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Sunk Cost is central. Confirmation Bias may make you search for reasons to justify continuing. All-or-Nothing Thinking can equate changing direction with total failure.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Build your own reality check. Identify the facts, assumptions, evidence for and against your view, and the missing information that could materially change the decision.\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The past investment cannot be recovered.\",\"The future cost of completing is still avoidable.\",\"My goals have changed.\",\"Some knowledge already gained may remain valuable even if I leave.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The past investment cannot be recovered.\",\"The future cost of completing is still avoidable.\",\"My goals have changed.\",\"Some knowledge already gained may remain valuable even if I leave.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate the realistic alternatives available to you. Include at least one option that is not your preferred choice and, where relevant, an option that changes the structure of the decision rather than simply choosing A or B.\",\"insight\":\"A decision can improve when you change the question from “Which option wins?” to “What options, conditions or safeguards could make the decision better?”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Finish because the qualification still supports the future.\",\"Leave because the opportunity cost is now too high.\",\"Pause if the program allows it.\",\"Redirect the remaining time toward a better-aligned skill.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Finish because the qualification still supports the future.\",\"Leave because the opportunity cost is now too high.\",\"Pause if the program allows it.\",\"Redirect the remaining time toward a better-aligned skill.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and why? If this is a decision rather than an immediate reaction, state what information, negotiation, experiment or safeguard should come before the final commitment.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Evaluate both paths from today forward.\",\"Compare remaining cost, likely future value and opportunity cost.\",\"Choose deliberately rather than continuing merely to justify the original decision.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Evaluate both paths from today forward.\\nCompare remaining cost, likely future value and opportunity cost.\\nChoose deliberately rather than continuing merely to justify the original decision.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “The judgment principle I want to carry forward is…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Changing direction is not automatically admitting failure; it can be a response to new information.\",\"reference_example\":\"Changing direction is not automatically admitting failure; it can be a response to new information.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"What decision would you make today if the past investment disappeared from the equation?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
