ment is difficult.\",\"Some decisions remain with the owners.\",\"You would be accountable for results.\",\"The role may materially affect your future career.\"],\"story\":\"This is the promotion I\'ve been waiting for. I should take it.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: The role carries a larger title and scope. The team is underperforming. The environment is difficult. Some decisions remain with the owners. You would be accountable for results. The role may materially affect your future career.\\nStory: This is the promotion I\'ve been waiting for. I should take it.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"primary_trap\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"Fortune Telling\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"all_or_nothing\",\"fortune_telling\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Validation Seeking can make title and recognition dominate the evaluation. All-or-Nothing Thinking can frame the choice as either taking the big opportunity or lacking ambition. Fortune Telling can assume the role will automatically accelerate the career.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Build your own reality check. Identify the facts, assumptions, evidence for and against your view, and the missing information that could materially change the decision.\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The opportunity is significant.\",\"Authority and accountability may not be aligned.\",\"Success expectations need clarification.\",\"The role\'s value depends on the actual operating conditions, not only the title.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The opportunity is significant.\",\"Authority and accountability may not be aligned.\",\"Success expectations need clarification.\",\"The role\'s value depends on the actual operating conditions, not only the title.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate the realistic alternatives available to you. Include at least one option that is not your preferred choice and, where relevant, an option that changes the structure of the decision rather than simply choosing A or B.\",\"insight\":\"A decision can improve when you change the question from “Which option wins?” to “What options, conditions or safeguards could make the decision better?”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The role may be excellent if authority is clarified.\",\"The role may be risky if accountability exceeds control.\",\"Terms could be negotiated.\",\"A different leadership role may offer better alignment.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The role may be excellent if authority is clarified.\",\"The role may be risky if accountability exceeds control.\",\"Terms could be negotiated.\",\"A different leadership role may offer better alignment.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and why? If this is a decision rather than an immediate reaction, state what information, negotiation, experiment or safeguard should come before the final commitment.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Map responsibility against decision rights.\",\"Clarify success metrics, resources, reporting, budget and owner involvement.\",\"Negotiate material gaps before deciding.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Map responsibility against decision rights.\\nClarify success metrics, resources, reporting, budget and owner involvement.\\nNegotiate material gaps before deciding.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “The judgment principle I want to carry forward is…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"A bigger responsibility requires enough authority and resources to carry it.\",\"reference_example\":\"A bigger responsibility requires enough authority and resources to carry it.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"When an opportunity looks impressive, what practical detail could you be overlooking?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (37, 2, 'The Founder Conflict', 'Business', 'Emotional Reasoning', 'Confirmation Bias, Mind Reading', '{\"day\":37,\"phase\":2,\"title\":\"The Founder Conflict\",\"domain\":\"Business\",\"mission\":\"Important decisions become harder when identity and evidence get mixed together.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Integrate Conflicting Evidence\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate–Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"5-7\",\"primary_skill\":\"Reframe\",\"primary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias, Mind Reading\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Mind Reading\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Low guidance; multi-variable judgment, competing values and uncertainty are central.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Defend → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You founded a business with a close friend.\\nThe business is growing, but you disagree about the next stage.\\nYou want to reinvest aggressively; your partner wants to preserve cash.\\nEach of you has examples that support your position.\\nThe disagreement has become personal, and both of you now question whether the other still trusts the partnership.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"Start without looking for the \'right\' answer. Write what you know, what you think it means, and what you are tempted to do.\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. The story explains what the mind thinks the facts mean.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story/assumptions your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"The business is growing.\",\"The founders disagree about reinvestment.\",\"Both have evidence supporting their position.\",\"The disagreement has become personal.\",\"The future cash requirement is uncertain.\"],\"story\":\"If my partner really believed in the business, they would support my plan.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: The business is growing. The founders disagree about reinvestment. Both have evidence supporting their position. The disagreement has become personal. The future cash requirement is uncertain.\\nStory: If my partner really believed in the business, they would support my plan.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"primary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Mind Reading\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"confirmation_bias\",\"mind_reading\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Emotional Reasoning can turn disagreement into evidence of disloyalty. Confirmation Bias makes each founder collect supporting examples. Mind Reading assigns an intention to the partner without verifying it.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Build your own reality check. Identify the facts, assumptions, evidence for and against your view, and the missing information that could materially change the decision.\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The disagreement is real.\",\"The reasons for each position can be examined.\",\"Trust and strategy are separate questions.\",\"The financial consequences of each path need to be quantified.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The disagreement is real.\",\"The reasons for each position can be examined.\",\"Trust and strategy are separate questions.\",\"The financial consequences of each path need to be quantified.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate the realistic alternatives available to you. Include at least one option that is not your preferred choice and, where relevant, an option that changes the structure of the decision rather than simply choosing A or B.\",\"insight\":\"A decision can improve when you change the question from “Which option wins?” to “What options, conditions or safeguards could make the decision better?”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The partner may be protecting the business from excessive risk.\",\"You may be seeing an opportunity the partner sees differently.\",\"Both positions may contain valid concerns.\",\"A staged investment plan could address both priorities.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The partner may be protecting the business from excessive risk.\",\"You may be seeing an opportunity the partner sees differently.\",\"Both positions may contain valid concerns.\",\"A staged investment plan could address both priorities.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and why? If this is a decision rather than an immediate reaction, state what information, negotiation, experiment or safeguard should come before the final commitment.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Separate the relationship conversation from the strategy conversation.\",\"Model the financial consequences of each option.\",\"Agree on decision criteria before arguing about the preferred option.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Separate the relationship conversation from the strategy conversation.\\nModel the financial consequences of each option.\\nAgree on decision criteria before arguing about the preferred option.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “The judgment principle I want to carry forward is…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Disagreement can be evidence of different risk judgments—not necessarily different commitment.\",\"reference_example\":\"Disagreement can be evidence of different risk judgments—not necessarily different commitment.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"When someone disagrees with you, what do you assume their disagreement means about you or the relationship?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
