mation Bias\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Catastrophizing\",\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"catastrophizing\",\"sunk_cost_fallacy\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Confirmation Bias can overvalue the brand and loyal customers while underweighting the financial evidence. Sunk Cost can make past investment feel like a reason to continue. Catastrophizing may also appear if stopping is framed as catastrophic failure.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Build your own reality check. Identify the facts, assumptions, evidence for and against your view, and the missing information that could materially change the decision.\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The brand has value.\",\"The current model has not produced sustainable financial performance.\",\"The turnaround requires additional resources.\",\"The decision depends on whether a credible path to sustainability exists.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The brand has value.\",\"The current model has not produced sustainable financial performance.\",\"The turnaround requires additional resources.\",\"The decision depends on whether a credible path to sustainability exists.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate the realistic alternatives available to you. Include at least one option that is not your preferred choice and, where relevant, an option that changes the structure of the decision rather than simply choosing A or B.\",\"insight\":\"A decision can improve when you change the question from “Which option wins?” to “What options, conditions or safeguards could make the decision better?”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Continue with a defined turnaround plan.\",\"Restructure the unit before investing further.\",\"Reduce the scope and test a focused model.\",\"Exit or redeploy resources if the economics cannot be repaired.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Continue with a defined turnaround plan.\",\"Restructure the unit before investing further.\",\"Reduce the scope and test a focused model.\",\"Exit or redeploy resources if the economics cannot be repaired.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and why? If this is a decision rather than an immediate reaction, state what information, negotiation, experiment or safeguard should come before the final commitment.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Build scenarios with explicit assumptions, milestones and stop criteria.\",\"Identify what evidence would show the turnaround is working.\",\"Present the options and trade-offs to the owners rather than advocating from attachment to the past.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Build scenarios with explicit assumptions, milestones and stop criteria.\\nIdentify what evidence would show the turnaround is working.\\nPresent the options and trade-offs to the owners rather than advocating from attachment to the past.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “The judgment principle I want to carry forward is…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"A valuable asset can still require a different strategy. Good judgment tests whether the future case is strong enough.\",\"reference_example\":\"A valuable asset can still require a different strategy. Good judgment tests whether the future case is strong enough.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Which fact would most change your view of this situation?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (40, 2, 'The Country Move', 'Life & Career', 'Fortune Telling', 'Validation Seeking, Sunk Cost Fallacy, Catastrophizing', '{\"day\":40,\"phase\":2,\"title\":\"The Country Move\",\"domain\":\"Life & Career\",\"mission\":\"Good judgment does not require perfect certainty.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Independent Application of the Complete Framework\",\"difficulty\":\"Intermediate–Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"5-7\",\"primary_skill\":\"Internalize\",\"primary_trap\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Validation Seeking, Sunk Cost Fallacy, Catastrophizing\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Validation Seeking\",\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"Catastrophizing\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Low guidance; multi-variable judgment, competing values and uncertainty are central.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Defend → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You have spent years building a stable career in one city.\\nYou now have an opportunity to move to another country for a substantially different career path.\\nThe opportunity could improve your professional trajectory and income.\\nIt would also mean leaving familiar routines, changing your partner\'s plans, rebuilding a social network and accepting uncertainty about how quickly the new career will develop.\\nThere is no guarantee that the move will work out.\\nThere is also no guarantee that staying will lead to the growth you want.\\nYou have enough information to begin the decision—but not enough to know the outcome.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"Start without looking for the \'right\' answer. Write what you know, what you think it means, and what you are tempted to do.\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. The story explains what the mind thinks the facts mean.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"story\",\"prompt\":\"Now write the story/assumptions your mind is creating.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"A relocation opportunity exists.\",\"It changes the career path and financial circumstances.\",\"It affects more than one person.\",\"There are meaningful benefits and costs.\",\"The future outcome cannot be known with certainty.\"],\"story\":\"User must generate their own story before seeing ThinkClear\'s analysis.\"},\"reference_example\":\"Fact: A relocation opportunity exists. It changes the career path and financial circumstances. It affects more than one person. There are meaningful benefits and costs. The future outcome cannot be known with certainty.\\nStory: User must generate their own story before seeing ThinkClear\'s analysis.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment? Select the one you think is primary and note any others.\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"primary_trap\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Validation Seeking\",\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"Catastrophizing\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"validation_seeking\",\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"catastrophizing\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Several traps can plausibly influence this decision. Fortune Telling may appear when an uncertain future is treated as knowable; Validation Seeking may make external success define the decision; Sunk Cost may make the existing career path feel binding; Catastrophizing may exaggerate the downside of either choice.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Build your own reality check. Identify the facts, assumptions, evidence for and against your view, and the missing information that could materially change the decision.\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"What is known?\",\"What is assumed?\",\"What information is still missing?\",\"Which assumptions would materially change the decision?\",\"What evidence would challenge the preferred option?\"],\"reference_example\":[\"What is known?\",\"What is assumed?\",\"What information is still missing?\",\"Which assumptions would materially change the decision?\",\"What evidence would challenge the preferred option?\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate the realistic alternatives available to you. Include at least one option that is not your preferred choice and, where relevant, an option that changes the structure of the decision rather than simply choosing A or B.\",\"insight\":\"A decision can improve when you change the question from “Which option wins?” to “What options, conditions or safeguards could make the decision better?”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Stay and pursue growth where you are.\",\"Relocate now.\",\"Negotiate a delayed or staged transition.\",\"Test the new path before making a full move, if feasible.\",\"Define conditions under which you would proceed or reconsider.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Stay and pursue growth where you are.\",\"Relocate now.\",\"Negotiate a delayed or staged transition.\",\"Test the new path before making a full move, if feasible.\",\"Define conditions under which you would proceed or reconsider.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and why? If this is a decision rather than an immediate reaction, state what information, negotiation, experiment or safeguard should come before the final commitment.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Build the decision around evidence, priorities, trade-offs, reversibility and missing information.\",\"State the decision, the reasons supporting it, the key assumptions and what would cause you to revisit it.\",\"Do not wait for certainty that no one can provide.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Build the decision around evidence, priorities, trade-offs, reversibility and missing information.\\nState the decision, the reasons supporting it, the key assumptions and what would cause you to revisit it.\\nDo not wait for certainty that no one can provide.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “The judgment principle I want to carry forward is…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Good judgment is not the ability to predict the future. It is the ability to make a reasoned choice under uncertainty and remain willing to update it when evidence changes.\",\"reference_example\":\"Good judgment is not the ability to predict the future. It is the ability to make a reasoned choice under uncertainty and remain willing to update it when evidence changes.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"When the outcome cannot be guaranteed, what does good judgment require from you?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}},\"end_of_phase2_walkthrough\":{\"summary\":\"Congratulations on completing Phase 2: Application (Days 21–40)!\",\"framework_milestone\":\"You have now mastered applying the 6-step framework to complex, multi-trap, high-stakes decisions with reduced scaffolding.\",\"unlocked_phase\":3,\"next_phase_title\":\"Phase 3: Decision Fitness (Days 41–60)\"}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
