ion\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"primary_trap\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Validation Seeking\",\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"Catastrophizing\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"validation_seeking\",\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"catastrophizing\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Several traps can plausibly influence this decision. Fortune Telling may appear when an uncertain future is treated as knowable; Validation Seeking may make external success define the decision; Sunk Cost may make the existing career path feel binding; Catastrophizing may exaggerate the downside of either choice.\\nRemember: More than one thinking trap can exist in the same situation. The goal is not to label yourself; it is to identify what may be distorting the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Build your own reality check. Identify the facts, assumptions, evidence for and against your view, and the missing information that could materially change the decision.\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What facts do you know for certain?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What assumptions are you making?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q3\",\"prompt\":\"3. What evidence supports your conclusion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q4\",\"prompt\":\"4. What evidence challenges it?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q5\",\"prompt\":\"5. What information is still missing?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"What is known?\",\"What is assumed?\",\"What information is still missing?\",\"Which assumptions would materially change the decision?\",\"What evidence would challenge the preferred option?\"],\"reference_example\":[\"What is known?\",\"What is assumed?\",\"What information is still missing?\",\"Which assumptions would materially change the decision?\",\"What evidence would challenge the preferred option?\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Generate the realistic alternatives available to you. Include at least one option that is not your preferred choice and, where relevant, an option that changes the structure of the decision rather than simply choosing A or B.\",\"insight\":\"A decision can improve when you change the question from “Which option wins?” to “What options, conditions or safeguards could make the decision better?”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"alt_explanations\",\"prompt\":\"Write at least four other explanations or perspectives that also fit the facts.\",\"type\":\"multi_entry\",\"min_entries\":4}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Stay and pursue growth where you are.\",\"Relocate now.\",\"Negotiate a delayed or staged transition.\",\"Test the new path before making a full move, if feasible.\",\"Define conditions under which you would proceed or reconsider.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Stay and pursue growth where you are.\",\"Relocate now.\",\"Negotiate a delayed or staged transition.\",\"Test the new path before making a full move, if feasible.\",\"Define conditions under which you would proceed or reconsider.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and why? If this is a decision rather than an immediate reaction, state what information, negotiation, experiment or safeguard should come before the final commitment.\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"Based on the evidence available today, what is the most reasonable next action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Build the decision around evidence, priorities, trade-offs, reversibility and missing information.\",\"State the decision, the reasons supporting it, the key assumptions and what would cause you to revisit it.\",\"Do not wait for certainty that no one can provide.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Build the decision around evidence, priorities, trade-offs, reversibility and missing information.\\nState the decision, the reasons supporting it, the key assumptions and what would cause you to revisit it.\\nDo not wait for certainty that no one can provide.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “The judgment principle I want to carry forward is…”\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"Complete the sentence: “Today I learned that…”\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Good judgment is not the ability to predict the future. It is the ability to make a reasoned choice under uncertainty and remain willing to update it when evidence changes.\",\"reference_example\":\"Good judgment is not the ability to predict the future. It is the ability to make a reasoned choice under uncertainty and remain willing to update it when evidence changes.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"When the outcome cannot be guaranteed, what does good judgment require from you?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}},\"end_of_phase2_walkthrough\":{\"summary\":\"Congratulations on completing Phase 2: Application (Days 21–40)!\",\"framework_milestone\":\"You have now mastered applying the 6-step framework to complex, multi-trap, high-stakes decisions with reduced scaffolding.\",\"unlocked_phase\":3,\"next_phase_title\":\"Phase 3: Decision Fitness (Days 41–60)\"}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (41, 3, 'The Declining Investment', 'Personal Finance', 'Sunk Cost Fallacy', 'Confirmation Bias, Emotional Reasoning, Fortune Telling', '{\"day\":41,\"phase\":3,\"title\":\"The Declining Investment\",\"domain\":\"Personal Finance\",\"mission\":\"Protecting your financial future sometimes means questioning an investment you once strongly believed in.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Evaluate concentrated financial risk, distinguish confidence from evidence, and recognise the opportunity cost of holding on to an investment.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"6-8\",\"primary_skill\":\"Evaluate\",\"primary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias, Emotional Reasoning, Fortune Telling\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"Fortune Telling\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate to high guidance; strategic leadership, financial risk and long-term consequences.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"Over the last four years, you have invested a significant portion of your savings in the shares of a company you believe has strong long-term potential.\\nYou initially invested because the company had a respected management team, a promising business model and a growing market.\\nThe share price has now fallen by 38% from your average purchase price.\\nYou have read several explanations for the decline:\\nSome analysts believe the fall is temporary and that the company is undervalued.\\nOthers have raised concerns about declining margins, increasing debt and stronger competition.\\nThe company\'s management continues to communicate confidence about its future.\\nA few investors who previously supported the company have started reducing their holdings.\\nYou have enough savings to manage your regular expenses, but this investment represents a substantial portion of the money you had set aside for a future property purchase.\\nYou now face a difficult choice.\\nSelling would convert the current paper loss into a realised loss. Holding could allow you to recover your investment if the company performs well, but it could also expose you to further losses and delay your property plans.\\nYou are not required to recover your original purchase price. You need to decide what makes financial sense from today onwards.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"What are the confirmed facts, and what are you assuming about the company\'s future?\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. Assumptions explain what the mind projects or fears.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the confirmed facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"assumptions\",\"prompt\":\"Write what you are assuming about this situation.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"The investment has declined by 38% from its average purchase price.\",\"It represents a substantial portion of the individual\'s savings.\",\"The money was intended partly for a future property purchase.\",\"There are conflicting views about the company\'s financial outlook.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"The share price will eventually recover.\",\"The decline is temporary.\",\"Selling now would necessarily be a bad decision.\",\"The company\'s management confidence guarantees future performance.\",\"The original purchase price is not evidence of what the investment is worth today.\"]},\"reference_example\":\"Confirmed facts: The investment has declined by 38% from its average purchase price.; It represents a substantial portion of the individual\'s savings.; The money was intended partly for a future property purchase.\\nAssumptions: The share price will eventually recover.; The decline is temporary.; Selling now would necessarily be a bad decision.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your decision, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"primary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"Fortune Telling\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"confirmation_bias\",\"emotional_reasoning\",\"fortune_telling\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Sunk Cost Fallacy\\nThe investor may continue holding the shares because of the money already invested, rather than evaluating whether holding remains the best decision today.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nConfirmation Bias: Giving greater importance to positive analyst opinions while overlooking negative financial indicators.\\nEmotional Reasoning: Treating the discomfort of accepting a loss as evidence that selling is wrong.\\nFortune Telling: Assuming the share price will eventually return to its earlier level.\\nOther interpretations may also be defensible depending on the investor\'s reasoning.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What evidence would help you determine whether holding the investment is still justified?\\n• What important information could materially change your decision?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What evidence would help you determine whether holding the investment is still justified?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What important information could materially change your decision?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Revenue growth and profitability trends.\",\"Debt levels and cash flow.\",\"Changes in the company\'s competitive position.\",\"Management\'s execution against previously communicated targets.\",\"Whether the original investment thesis remains valid.\",\"The investor\'s current financial goals and time horizon.\",\"The most important question is not whether the share price can recover.\",\"It is whether this investment still offers an attractive risk-adjusted opportunity compared with the alternatives available today.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Revenue growth and profitability trends.\",\"Debt levels and cash flow.\",\"Changes in the company\'s competitive position.\",\"Management\'s execution against previously communicated targets.\",\"Whether the original investment thesis remains valid.\",\"The investor\'s current financial goals and time horizon.\",\"The most important question is not whether the share price can recover.\",\"It is whether this investment still offers an attractive risk-adjusted opportunity compared with the alternatives available today.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What realistic options do you have beyond simply holding everything or selling everything?\\n• How could you restructure the decision to protect your financial goals while retaining some potential upside?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What realistic options do you have beyond simply holding everything or selling everything?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you restructure the decision to protect your financial goals while retaining some potential upside?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Continue holding if the business fundamentals remain strong and the risk is acceptable.\",\"Sell part of the investment to reduce concentration risk.\",\"Exit if the original investment thesis is no longer supported.\",\"Retain a smaller position while redirecting money needed for the property goal.\",\"Establish objective conditions for reviewing or exiting the investment.\",\"A partial exit may be more appropriate than treating the decision as an absolute choice between holding everything and selling everything.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Continue holding if the business fundamentals remain strong and the risk is acceptable.\",\"Sell part of the investment to reduce concentration risk.\",\"Exit if the original investment thesis is no longer supported.\",\"Retain a smaller position while redirecting money needed for the property goal.\",\"Establish objective conditions for reviewing or exiting the investment.\",\"A partial exit may be more appropriate than treating the decision as an absolute choice between holding everything and selling everything.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and what evidence would justify your decision?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and what evidence would justify your decision?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Review the company\'s financial performance rather than relying on market commentary.\",\"Separate money required for near-term goals from long-term investment capital.\",\"Calculate the impact of different holding and selling scenarios.\",\"Decide an acceptable level of exposure.\",\"Establish a review date and specific conditions that would change the decision.\",\"Avoid making the decision solely to escape the discomfort of seeing a loss.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Review the company\'s financial performance rather than relying on market commentary.\\nSeparate money required for near-term goals from long-term investment capital.\\nCalculate the impact of different holding and selling scenarios.\\nDecide an acceptable level of exposure.\\nEstablish a review date and specific conditions that would change the decision.\\nAvoid making the decision solely to escape the discomfort of seeing a loss.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"An investment should be evaluated on its future merits, not defended merely because money has already been committed to it.\",\"reference_example\":\"An investment should be evaluated on its future merits, not defended merely because money has already been committed to it.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"If you had never purchased these shares, would you invest the same amount in this company today?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE `title` = 'The Declining Investment', `domain` = 'Personal Finance', `primary_trap` = 'Sunk Cost Fallacy', `secondary_trap` = 'Confirmation Bias, Emotional Reasoning, Fortune Telling', `content_bundle` = '{\"day\":41,\"phase\":3,\"title\":\"The Declining Investment\",\"domain\":\"Personal Finance\",\"mission\":\"Protecting your financial future sometimes means questioning an investment you once strongly believed in.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Evaluate concentrated financial risk, distinguish confidence from evidence, and recognise the opportunity cost of holding on to an investment.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"6-8\",\"primary_skill\":\"Evaluate\",\"primary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias, Emotional Reasoning, Fortune Telling\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"Fortune Telling\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate to high guidance; strategic leadership, financial risk and long-term consequences.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"Over the last four years, you have invested a significant portion of your savings in the shares of a company you believe has strong long-term potential.\\nYou initially invested because the company had a respected management team, a promising business model and a growing market.\\nThe share price has now fallen by 38% from your average purchase price.\\nYou have read several explanations for the decline:\\nSome analysts believe the fall is temporary and that the company is undervalued.\\nOthers have raised concerns about declining margins, increasing debt and stronger competition.\\nThe company\'s management continues to communicate confidence about its future.\\nA few investors who previously supported the company have started reducing their holdings.\\nYou have enough savings to manage your regular expenses, but this investment represents a substantial portion of the money you had set aside for a future property purchase.\\nYou now face a difficult choice.\\nSelling would convert the current paper loss into a realised loss. Holding could allow you to recover your investment if the company performs well, but it could also expose you to further losses and delay your property plans.\\nYou are not required to recover your original purchase price. You need to decide what makes financial sense from today onwards.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"What are the confirmed facts, and what are you assuming about the company\'s future?\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. Assumptions explain what the mind projects or fears.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the confirmed facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"assumptions\",\"prompt\":\"Write what you are assuming about this situation.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"The investment has declined by 38% from its average purchase price.\",\"It represents a substantial portion of the individual\'s savings.\",\"The money was intended partly for a future property purchase.\",\"There are conflicting views about the company\'s financial outlook.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"The share price will eventually recover.\",\"The decline is temporary.\",\"Selling now would necessarily be a bad decision.\",\"The company\'s management confidence guarantees future performance.\",\"The original purchase price is not evidence of what the investment is worth today.\"]},\"reference_example\":\"Confirmed facts: The investment has declined by 38% from its average purchase price.; It represents a substantial portion of the individual\'s savings.; The money was intended partly for a future property purchase.\\nAssumptions: The share price will eventually recover.; The decline is temporary.; Selling now would necessarily be a bad decision.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your decision, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"primary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"Fortune Telling\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"confirmation_bias\",\"emotional_reasoning\",\"fortune_telling\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Sunk Cost Fallacy\\nThe investor may continue holding the shares because of the money already invested, rather than evaluating whether holding remains the best decision today.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nConfirmation Bias: Giving greater importance to positive analyst opinions while overlooking negative financial indicators.\\nEmotional Reasoning: Treating the discomfort of accepting a loss as evidence that selling is wrong.\\nFortune Telling: Assuming the share price will eventually return to its earlier level.\\nOther interpretations may also be defensible depending on the investor\'s reasoning.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What evidence would help you determine whether holding the investment is still justified?\\n• What important information could materially change your decision?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What evidence would help you determine whether holding the investment is still justified?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What important information could materially change your decision?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Revenue growth and profitability trends.\",\"Debt levels and cash flow.\",\"Changes in the company\'s competitive position.\",\"Management\'s execution against previously communicated targets.\",\"Whether the original investment thesis remains valid.\",\"The investor\'s current financial goals and time horizon.\",\"The most important question is not whether the share price can recover.\",\"It is whether this investment still offers an attractive risk-adjusted opportunity compared with the alternatives available today.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Revenue growth and profitability trends.\",\"Debt levels and cash flow.\",\"Changes in the company\'s competitive position.\",\"Management\'s execution against previously communicated targets.\",\"Whether the original investment thesis remains valid.\",\"The investor\'s current financial goals and time horizon.\",\"The most important question is not whether the share price can recover.\",\"It is whether this investment still offers an attractive risk-adjusted opportunity compared with the alternatives available today.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What realistic options do you have beyond simply holding everything or selling everything?\\n• How could you restructure the decision to protect your financial goals while retaining some potential upside?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What realistic options do you have beyond simply holding everything or selling everything?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you restructure the decision to protect your financial goals while retaining some potential upside?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Continue holding if the business fundamentals remain strong and the risk is acceptable.\",\"Sell part of the investment to reduce concentration risk.\",\"Exit if the original investment thesis is no longer supported.\",\"Retain a smaller position while redirecting money needed for the property goal.\",\"Establish objective conditions for reviewing or exiting the investment.\",\"A partial exit may be more appropriate than treating the decision as an absolute choice between holding everything and selling everything.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Continue holding if the business fundamentals remain strong and the risk is acceptable.\",\"Sell part of the investment to reduce concentration risk.\",\"Exit if the original investment thesis is no longer supported.\",\"Retain a smaller position while redirecting money needed for the property goal.\",\"Establish objective conditions for reviewing or exiting the investment.\",\"A partial exit may be more appropriate than treating the decision as an absolute choice between holding everything and selling everything.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and what evidence would justify your decision?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and what evidence would justify your decision?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Review the company\'s financial performance rather than relying on market commentary.\",\"Separate money required for near-term goals from long-term investment capital.\",\"Calculate the impact of different holding and selling scenarios.\",\"Decide an acceptable level of exposure.\",\"Establish a review date and specific conditions that would change the decision.\",\"Avoid making the decision solely to escape the discomfort of seeing a loss.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Review the company\'s financial performance rather than relying on market commentary.\\nSeparate money required for near-term goals from long-term investment capital.\\nCalculate the impact of different holding and selling scenarios.\\nDecide an acceptable level of exposure.\\nEstablish a review date and specific conditions that would change the decision.\\nAvoid making the decision solely to escape the discomfort of seeing a loss.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"An investment should be evaluated on its future merits, not defended merely because money has already been committed to it.\",\"reference_example\":\"An investment should be evaluated on its future merits, not defended merely because money has already been committed to it.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"If you had never purchased these shares, would you invest the same amount in this company today?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (42, 3, 'The Commercial Property Purchase', 'Financial Decisions / Property', 'Fortune Telling', 'Validation Seeking, Catastrophizing, Confirmation Bias', '{\"day\":42,\"phase\":3,\"title\":\"The Commercial Property Purchase\",\"domain\":\"Financial Decisions / Property\",\"mission\":\"A major purchase should be justified by its long-term value, not by the fear of missing an opportunity.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Evaluate irreversible commitments, distinguish investment fundamentals from market pressure, and understand the cost of premature decisions.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"6-8\",\"primary_skill\":\"Evaluate\",\"primary_trap\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Validation Seeking, Catastrophizing, Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Validation Seeking\",\"Catastrophizing\",\"Confirmation Bias\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate to high guidance; strategic leadership, financial risk and long-term consequences.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You have been considering purchasing a commercial property for several months.\\nThe property is located in an area that is expected to develop over the next five years. A new infrastructure project has been announced nearby, and several commercial developments are planned.\\nThe seller is asking ₹1.8 crore.\\nYou have ₹45 lakh available for the down payment and would need to take a substantial loan for the remaining amount.\\nThe property is currently vacant. The seller claims that a tenant could be found easily once the surrounding developments are completed.\\nYou have not independently verified the rental demand or the likely rental value.\\nYour family believes that property is a safer long-term investment than keeping money in financial markets. A broker has also told you that the seller has received interest from another buyer and expects a decision within a week.\\nYou like the property and believe it could appreciate significantly.\\nHowever:\\nThe loan would increase your monthly financial commitments.\\nRental income is not guaranteed.\\nDevelopment in the surrounding area may take longer than expected.\\nThe money used for the down payment would reduce your financial flexibility.\\nYou have other possible uses for this capital.\\nYou must decide whether to proceed, renegotiate, wait or walk away.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"What are the confirmed facts, and what are you assuming about the property\'s future value and rental potential?\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. Assumptions explain what the mind projects or fears.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the confirmed facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"assumptions\",\"prompt\":\"Write what you are assuming about this situation.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"The seller is asking ₹1.8 crore.\",\"The buyer has ₹45 lakh available.\",\"A substantial loan would be required.\",\"The property is vacant.\",\"Nearby infrastructure and commercial development have been announced.\",\"Rental demand and future appreciation have not been independently established.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"The property will appreciate significantly.\",\"Tenants will be easy to find.\",\"The infrastructure project will be completed on schedule.\",\"Buying now is better than waiting.\",\"The property will generate sufficient returns to justify the borrowing cost.\"]},\"reference_example\":\"Confirmed facts: The seller is asking ₹1.8 crore.; The buyer has ₹45 lakh available.; A substantial loan would be required.\\nAssumptions: The property will appreciate significantly.; Tenants will be easy to find.; The infrastructure project will be completed on schedule.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your decision, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"primary_trap\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Validation Seeking\",\"Catastrophizing\",\"Confirmation Bias\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"validation_seeking\",\"catastrophizing\",\"confirmation_bias\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Fortune Telling\\nThe buyer may be treating future appreciation and rental demand as predictable outcomes rather than uncertain possibilities.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nValidation Seeking: Family and broker opinions may be influencing the decision.\\nCatastrophizing: The buyer may believe that not purchasing now means permanently missing the opportunity.\\nConfirmation Bias: Focusing on infrastructure announcements while overlooking the property\'s current economics.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What financial and market evidence should be examined before committing?\\n• Which assumption, if proven wrong, could make this purchase financially unattractive?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What financial and market evidence should be examined before committing?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. Which assumption, if proven wrong, could make this purchase financially unattractive?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Independent valuation of the property.\",\"Actual transaction prices of comparable properties.\",\"Realistic rental rates and current vacancy levels.\",\"Total loan repayment and interest cost.\",\"Property taxes, maintenance and transaction costs.\",\"Legal title, approvals and permitted commercial use.\",\"Realistic timelines for infrastructure completion.\",\"One particularly important assumption is that rental income or capital appreciation will justify the cost of borrowing.\",\"If neither materialises, the buyer may be left with a large financial commitment and an illiquid asset.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Independent valuation of the property.\",\"Actual transaction prices of comparable properties.\",\"Realistic rental rates and current vacancy levels.\",\"Total loan repayment and interest cost.\",\"Property taxes, maintenance and transaction costs.\",\"Legal title, approvals and permitted commercial use.\",\"Realistic timelines for infrastructure completion.\",\"One particularly important assumption is that rental income or capital appreciation will justify the cost of borrowing.\",\"If neither materialises, the buyer may be left with a large financial commitment and an illiquid asset.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What realistic alternatives exist apart from purchasing immediately or abandoning the opportunity?\\n• How could you change the structure of the decision to reduce the financial risk?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What realistic alternatives exist apart from purchasing immediately or abandoning the opportunity?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you change the structure of the decision to reduce the financial risk?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Negotiate a lower purchase price based on comparable transactions.\",\"Wait until infrastructure progress and rental demand become clearer.\",\"Explore a smaller property with lower financial exposure.\",\"Consider renting commercial space rather than purchasing.\",\"Seek a lease or other arrangement that provides access without a major capital commitment.\",\"Proceed only if the property\'s current economics justify the purchase without depending entirely on future appreciation.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Negotiate a lower purchase price based on comparable transactions.\",\"Wait until infrastructure progress and rental demand become clearer.\",\"Explore a smaller property with lower financial exposure.\",\"Consider renting commercial space rather than purchasing.\",\"Seek a lease or other arrangement that provides access without a major capital commitment.\",\"Proceed only if the property\'s current economics justify the purchase without depending entirely on future appreciation.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next before making the final commitment?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next before making the final commitment?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Obtain an independent property valuation.\",\"Conduct legal due diligence.\",\"Calculate total ownership and financing costs.\",\"Estimate rental returns using realistic local evidence.\",\"Stress-test the decision against delayed development, prolonged vacancy and higher borrowing costs.\",\"Establish a maximum purchase price and a limit on acceptable monthly financial exposure.\",\"Do not let the seller\'s deadline replace your due diligence.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Obtain an independent property valuation.\\nConduct legal due diligence.\\nCalculate total ownership and financing costs.\\nEstimate rental returns using realistic local evidence.\\nStress-test the decision against delayed development, prolonged vacancy and higher borrowing costs.\\nEstablish a maximum purchase price and a limit on acceptable monthly financial exposure.\\nDo not let the seller\'s deadline replace your due diligence.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"A good investment should make financial sense under realistic assumptions, not only under an optimistic prediction of the future.\",\"reference_example\":\"A good investment should make financial sense under realistic assumptions, not only under an optimistic prediction of the future.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Would you still purchase this property if you knew its value would remain unchanged for the next five years?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
