) may be influencing your decision, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"primary_trap\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Validation Seeking\",\"Catastrophizing\",\"Confirmation Bias\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"validation_seeking\",\"catastrophizing\",\"confirmation_bias\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Fortune Telling\\nThe buyer may be treating future appreciation and rental demand as predictable outcomes rather than uncertain possibilities.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nValidation Seeking: Family and broker opinions may be influencing the decision.\\nCatastrophizing: The buyer may believe that not purchasing now means permanently missing the opportunity.\\nConfirmation Bias: Focusing on infrastructure announcements while overlooking the property\'s current economics.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What financial and market evidence should be examined before committing?\\n• Which assumption, if proven wrong, could make this purchase financially unattractive?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What financial and market evidence should be examined before committing?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. Which assumption, if proven wrong, could make this purchase financially unattractive?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Independent valuation of the property.\",\"Actual transaction prices of comparable properties.\",\"Realistic rental rates and current vacancy levels.\",\"Total loan repayment and interest cost.\",\"Property taxes, maintenance and transaction costs.\",\"Legal title, approvals and permitted commercial use.\",\"Realistic timelines for infrastructure completion.\",\"One particularly important assumption is that rental income or capital appreciation will justify the cost of borrowing.\",\"If neither materialises, the buyer may be left with a large financial commitment and an illiquid asset.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Independent valuation of the property.\",\"Actual transaction prices of comparable properties.\",\"Realistic rental rates and current vacancy levels.\",\"Total loan repayment and interest cost.\",\"Property taxes, maintenance and transaction costs.\",\"Legal title, approvals and permitted commercial use.\",\"Realistic timelines for infrastructure completion.\",\"One particularly important assumption is that rental income or capital appreciation will justify the cost of borrowing.\",\"If neither materialises, the buyer may be left with a large financial commitment and an illiquid asset.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What realistic alternatives exist apart from purchasing immediately or abandoning the opportunity?\\n• How could you change the structure of the decision to reduce the financial risk?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What realistic alternatives exist apart from purchasing immediately or abandoning the opportunity?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you change the structure of the decision to reduce the financial risk?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Negotiate a lower purchase price based on comparable transactions.\",\"Wait until infrastructure progress and rental demand become clearer.\",\"Explore a smaller property with lower financial exposure.\",\"Consider renting commercial space rather than purchasing.\",\"Seek a lease or other arrangement that provides access without a major capital commitment.\",\"Proceed only if the property\'s current economics justify the purchase without depending entirely on future appreciation.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Negotiate a lower purchase price based on comparable transactions.\",\"Wait until infrastructure progress and rental demand become clearer.\",\"Explore a smaller property with lower financial exposure.\",\"Consider renting commercial space rather than purchasing.\",\"Seek a lease or other arrangement that provides access without a major capital commitment.\",\"Proceed only if the property\'s current economics justify the purchase without depending entirely on future appreciation.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next before making the final commitment?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next before making the final commitment?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Obtain an independent property valuation.\",\"Conduct legal due diligence.\",\"Calculate total ownership and financing costs.\",\"Estimate rental returns using realistic local evidence.\",\"Stress-test the decision against delayed development, prolonged vacancy and higher borrowing costs.\",\"Establish a maximum purchase price and a limit on acceptable monthly financial exposure.\",\"Do not let the seller\'s deadline replace your due diligence.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Obtain an independent property valuation.\\nConduct legal due diligence.\\nCalculate total ownership and financing costs.\\nEstimate rental returns using realistic local evidence.\\nStress-test the decision against delayed development, prolonged vacancy and higher borrowing costs.\\nEstablish a maximum purchase price and a limit on acceptable monthly financial exposure.\\nDo not let the seller\'s deadline replace your due diligence.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"A good investment should make financial sense under realistic assumptions, not only under an optimistic prediction of the future.\",\"reference_example\":\"A good investment should make financial sense under realistic assumptions, not only under an optimistic prediction of the future.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Would you still purchase this property if you knew its value would remain unchanged for the next five years?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (43, 3, 'Expanding into a Second Location', 'Business / Entrepreneurship', 'Fortune Telling', 'Catastrophizing, Confirmation Bias, Validation Seeking', '{\"day\":43,\"phase\":3,\"title\":\"Expanding into a Second Location\",\"domain\":\"Business / Entrepreneurship\",\"mission\":\"Growth is not always progress when the financial foundation cannot support it.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Evaluate expansion under financial pressure, distinguish revenue growth from sustainable growth, and recognise when ambition must be balanced with financial discipline.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"6-8\",\"primary_skill\":\"Evaluate\",\"primary_trap\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Catastrophizing, Confirmation Bias, Validation Seeking\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Catastrophizing\",\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Validation Seeking\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate to high guidance; strategic leadership, financial risk and long-term consequences.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You own a profitable service business that has been operating successfully for four years.\\nThe business generates approximately ₹30 lakh in monthly revenue and has a stable customer base.\\nYou have now identified an opportunity to expand into a second location.\\nThe new location has good visibility, a potentially attractive customer base and relatively limited competition.\\nThe expansion would require:\\n₹60 lakh in initial investment.\\nAdditional recruitment and training.\\nHigher monthly operating expenses.\\nA loan to finance part of the investment.\\nA consultant estimates that the new location could generate ₹20 lakh in monthly revenue within its first year.\\nHowever, this estimate is based on market potential rather than an actual customer pipeline.\\nYour existing business is profitable, but its cash reserves are limited because a significant amount of capital is tied up in receivables and ongoing operations.\\nYour business partner supports expansion and believes that waiting will allow competitors to capture the market.\\nYour finance manager recommends strengthening the existing business first, improving collections and building a larger cash reserve.\\nYou are attracted to the growth opportunity, but you also know that a failed expansion could affect the stability of your existing business.\\nThe decision is no longer simply about whether the second location is attractive.\\nIt is about whether the organisation can afford to pursue it now.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"What are the confirmed facts, and what are you assuming about the new location\'s ability to generate profitable growth?\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. Assumptions explain what the mind projects or fears.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the confirmed facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"assumptions\",\"prompt\":\"Write what you are assuming about this situation.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"The existing business generates ₹30 lakh in monthly revenue.\",\"The business is currently profitable.\",\"The proposed expansion requires ₹60 lakh in initial investment.\",\"Part of the investment would be debt-funded.\",\"The projected ₹20 lakh monthly revenue is an estimate, not an established result.\",\"Existing cash reserves are limited.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"The new location will attract enough customers.\",\"The revenue projection is achievable within one year.\",\"The existing business can absorb the financial pressure.\",\"Delaying expansion will allow competitors to capture the opportunity.\"]},\"reference_example\":\"Confirmed facts: The existing business generates ₹30 lakh in monthly revenue.; The business is currently profitable.; The proposed expansion requires ₹60 lakh in initial investment.\\nAssumptions: The new location will attract enough customers.; The revenue projection is achievable within one year.; The existing business can absorb the financial pressure.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your decision, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"primary_trap\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Catastrophizing\",\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Validation Seeking\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"catastrophizing\",\"confirmation_bias\",\"validation_seeking\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Fortune Telling\\nThe projected revenue is being treated as a likely outcome without sufficient validation.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nCatastrophizing: The belief that delaying expansion will necessarily result in losing the market.\\nConfirmation Bias: Giving more attention to the consultant\'s optimistic projection than to the finance manager\'s concerns.\\nValidation Seeking: Allowing the business partner\'s enthusiasm or approval to influence the decision.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What evidence would establish whether the second location can become financially sustainable?\\n• What could happen to the existing business if the expansion underperforms?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What evidence would establish whether the second location can become financially sustainable?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What could happen to the existing business if the expansion underperforms?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"The decision requires examination of:\",\"Actual customer demand and competitor activity.\",\"Expected customer acquisition costs.\",\"Break-even revenue and monthly fixed costs.\",\"Recruitment, training and operational readiness.\",\"Loan repayment obligations.\",\"Working capital requirements.\",\"Existing business cash flow and receivables.\",\"The financial impact of a six-to-twelve-month delay in achieving projected revenue.\",\"The second location may be commercially attractive but financially premature.\",\"The distinction between profitability and cash availability is critical. A profitable business can still face serious liquidity pressure.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"The decision requires examination of:\",\"Actual customer demand and competitor activity.\",\"Expected customer acquisition costs.\",\"Break-even revenue and monthly fixed costs.\",\"Recruitment, training and operational readiness.\",\"Loan repayment obligations.\",\"Working capital requirements.\",\"Existing business cash flow and receivables.\",\"The financial impact of a six-to-twelve-month delay in achieving projected revenue.\",\"The second location may be commercially attractive but financially premature.\",\"The distinction between profitability and cash availability is critical. A profitable business can still face serious liquidity pressure.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What alternatives exist apart from expanding immediately or abandoning the opportunity?\\n• How could you test the opportunity without exposing the entire existing business to the expansion risk?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What alternatives exist apart from expanding immediately or abandoning the opportunity?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you test the opportunity without exposing the entire existing business to the expansion risk?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Proceed with the full expansion after securing adequate funding.\",\"Delay expansion until collections and cash reserves improve.\",\"Start with a smaller operational model.\",\"Pilot the service through a temporary or shared facility.\",\"Negotiate a phased lease or investment commitment.\",\"Validate customer demand before committing to the full capital expenditure.\",\"Set financial milestones that must be achieved before moving to the next stage.\",\"The decision can be redesigned as a staged investment rather than a single large commitment.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Proceed with the full expansion after securing adequate funding.\",\"Delay expansion until collections and cash reserves improve.\",\"Start with a smaller operational model.\",\"Pilot the service through a temporary or shared facility.\",\"Negotiate a phased lease or investment commitment.\",\"Validate customer demand before committing to the full capital expenditure.\",\"Set financial milestones that must be achieved before moving to the next stage.\",\"The decision can be redesigned as a staged investment rather than a single large commitment.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and what conditions would need to be satisfied before approving expansion?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and what conditions would need to be satisfied before approving expansion?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Preparing optimistic, realistic and pessimistic financial projections.\",\"Establishing a minimum cash reserve for the existing business.\",\"Calculating the break-even point of the new location.\",\"Validating demand through actual customer commitments or a pilot.\",\"Setting a maximum acceptable debt level.\",\"Defining clear performance milestones and an exit condition.\",\"Expansion should proceed only when the organisation has both a credible business opportunity and the financial capacity to execute it.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Preparing optimistic, realistic and pessimistic financial projections.\\nEstablishing a minimum cash reserve for the existing business.\\nCalculating the break-even point of the new location.\\nValidating demand through actual customer commitments or a pilot.\\nSetting a maximum acceptable debt level.\\nDefining clear performance milestones and an exit condition.\\nExpansion should proceed only when the organisation has both a credible business opportunity and the financial capacity to execute it.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Growth should strengthen the business, not put its existing stability at risk.\",\"reference_example\":\"Growth should strengthen the business, not put its existing stability at risk.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"If the new location takes twice as long as expected to become profitable, would your business still be able to survive comfortably?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
