 Thinking: Believing that delegation means surrendering control completely.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What evidence would help you determine which decisions genuinely require founder involvement?\\n• How could you evaluate whether the current management structure is creating an organisational bottleneck?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What evidence would help you determine which decisions genuinely require founder involvement?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you evaluate whether the current management structure is creating an organisational bottleneck?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Number of decisions awaiting founder approval.\",\"Time taken to resolve routine issues.\",\"Manager capability assessments.\",\"Frequency of operational errors.\",\"Existing financial controls and approval limits.\",\"Quality and service performance across locations.\",\"Time spent on strategic versus routine activities.\",\"A critical distinction exists between accountability and personal approval of every decision.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Number of decisions awaiting founder approval.\",\"Time taken to resolve routine issues.\",\"Manager capability assessments.\",\"Frequency of operational errors.\",\"Existing financial controls and approval limits.\",\"Quality and service performance across locations.\",\"Time spent on strategic versus routine activities.\",\"A critical distinction exists between accountability and personal approval of every decision.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What alternatives exist between complete centralisation and unrestricted delegation?\\n• How could you design a system that allows managers to act independently while maintaining organisational control?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What alternatives exist between complete centralisation and unrestricted delegation?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you design a system that allows managers to act independently while maintaining organisational control?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Introduce a delegation of authority matrix.\",\"Establish financial approval thresholds.\",\"Define standard operating procedures.\",\"Create performance dashboards.\",\"Delegate decisions with clear accountability.\",\"Introduce exception-based reporting.\",\"Develop managers through structured coaching.\",\"Conduct periodic internal audits.\",\"The objective is not to remove the founder from operations. It is to make the organisation less dependent on the founder.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Introduce a delegation of authority matrix.\",\"Establish financial approval thresholds.\",\"Define standard operating procedures.\",\"Create performance dashboards.\",\"Delegate decisions with clear accountability.\",\"Introduce exception-based reporting.\",\"Develop managers through structured coaching.\",\"Conduct periodic internal audits.\",\"The objective is not to remove the founder from operations. It is to make the organisation less dependent on the founder.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you delegate first, and how would you monitor the results?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What would you delegate first, and how would you monitor the results?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Identifying recurring decisions that do not require CEO approval.\",\"Assigning authority to competent managers.\",\"Defining limits and escalation conditions.\",\"Establishing measurable performance indicators.\",\"Reviewing exceptions rather than micromanaging routine activity.\",\"Conducting monthly management reviews.\",\"Delegation without accountability is risky. Accountability without authority is equally ineffective.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Identifying recurring decisions that do not require CEO approval.\\nAssigning authority to competent managers.\\nDefining limits and escalation conditions.\\nEstablishing measurable performance indicators.\\nReviewing exceptions rather than micromanaging routine activity.\\nConducting monthly management reviews.\\nDelegation without accountability is risky. Accountability without authority is equally ineffective.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"A business becomes scalable when its systems and people can deliver results without requiring the founder\'s constant intervention.\",\"reference_example\":\"A business becomes scalable when its systems and people can deliver results without requiring the founder\'s constant intervention.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"If your business cannot function effectively for 30 days without you, have you built an organisation or simply created a demanding job for yourself?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (49, 3, 'The Client Who Wants You to Compromise Your Standards', 'Entrepreneurship / Business Ethics / Client Management', 'Sunk Cost Fallacy', 'Validation Seeking, Catastrophizing, Rationalisation', '{\"day\":49,\"phase\":3,\"title\":\"The Client Who Wants You to Compromise Your Standards\",\"domain\":\"Entrepreneurship / Business Ethics / Client Management\",\"mission\":\"Short-term commercial gains should not require compromising the principles on which your business depends.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Recognise ethical pressure in commercial relationships, evaluate reputational exposure and make decisions when revenue conflicts with professional standards.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"6-8\",\"primary_skill\":\"Evaluate\",\"primary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Validation Seeking, Catastrophizing, Rationalisation\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Validation Seeking\",\"Catastrophizing\",\"Rationalisation\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate to high guidance; strategic leadership, financial risk and long-term consequences.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You run a professional consulting firm that has recently secured an opportunity to work with a large corporate client.\\nThe contract could generate ₹1.5 crore in annual revenue and provide access to several future business opportunities.\\nDuring contract discussions, the client\'s procurement head privately suggests that a personal commission would help ensure your company\'s selection and smooth approval of future invoices.\\nHe indicates that similar arrangements are common in the industry.\\nYour sales director recommends accepting the arrangement indirectly through a third-party consultant.\\nHe argues that losing the opportunity would put the company at a disadvantage against competitors.\\nYour finance head is uncomfortable because the proposed payment cannot be justified by any legitimate service.\\nYou have already invested considerable time and money in securing this client.\\nWalking away could affect the company\'s growth targets and employee confidence.\\nYou must decide whether to proceed, challenge the demand, restructure the relationship or withdraw from the opportunity.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"What are the confirmed facts, and what are you assuming about the commercial consequences of refusing the demand?\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. Assumptions explain what the mind projects or fears.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the confirmed facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"assumptions\",\"prompt\":\"Write what you are assuming about this situation.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"The proposed contract is commercially significant.\",\"A personal commission has been suggested.\",\"No legitimate service justifies the proposed payment.\",\"Internal stakeholders disagree about the response.\",\"The company has already invested resources in securing the contract.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"The payment is necessary to secure the contract.\",\"Competitors will accept the same arrangement.\",\"Refusing the demand will permanently close the opportunity.\",\"Using an intermediary will remove responsibility from your company.\",\"The commercial attractiveness of an opportunity does not establish the legitimacy of the means used to secure it.\"]},\"reference_example\":\"Confirmed facts: The proposed contract is commercially significant.; A personal commission has been suggested.; No legitimate service justifies the proposed payment.\\nAssumptions: The payment is necessary to secure the contract.; Competitors will accept the same arrangement.; Refusing the demand will permanently close the opportunity.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"primary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Validation Seeking\",\"Catastrophizing\",\"Rationalisation\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"validation_seeking\",\"catastrophizing\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Sunk Cost Fallacy\\nThe company may feel compelled to accept the demand because of the time and resources already invested in winning the contract.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nSocial Validation Seeking: Justifying the conduct because it is supposedly common in the industry.\\nCatastrophizing: Believing that refusal will seriously threaten the business.\\nRationalisation: Reinterpreting an improper payment as an ordinary commercial expense.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What legal, financial and reputational risks should be evaluated before proceeding?\\n• What information would help distinguish a legitimate commercial arrangement from an improper personal benefit?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What legal, financial and reputational risks should be evaluated before proceeding?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What information would help distinguish a legitimate commercial arrangement from an improper personal benefit?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Relevant considerations include:\",\"Applicable anti-corruption laws.\",\"Company policies and procurement requirements.\",\"Whether a legitimate service is being provided.\",\"Beneficial ownership of intermediaries.\",\"Accounting and tax treatment.\",\"Potential reputational damage.\",\"Contractual and regulatory exposure.\",\"The possibility of reporting the demand through appropriate channels.\",\"The use of an intermediary does not automatically remove the company\'s legal or ethical responsibility.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Relevant considerations include:\",\"Applicable anti-corruption laws.\",\"Company policies and procurement requirements.\",\"Whether a legitimate service is being provided.\",\"Beneficial ownership of intermediaries.\",\"Accounting and tax treatment.\",\"Potential reputational damage.\",\"Contractual and regulatory exposure.\",\"The possibility of reporting the demand through appropriate channels.\",\"The use of an intermediary does not automatically remove the company\'s legal or ethical responsibility.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What alternatives exist beyond accepting the payment demand or immediately abandoning all commercial discussions?\\n• How could you protect the business opportunity while maintaining ethical standards?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What alternatives exist beyond accepting the payment demand or immediately abandoning all commercial discussions?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you protect the business opportunity while maintaining ethical standards?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Reject the personal payment demand.\",\"Request a transparent and documented procurement process.\",\"Offer legitimate commercial discounts where justified.\",\"Escalate the concern to the client\'s appropriate senior authority or compliance function.\",\"Seek legal advice.\",\"Withdraw if the client insists on improper conduct.\",\"The objective is to distinguish a legitimate commercial negotiation from an unethical demand.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Reject the personal payment demand.\",\"Request a transparent and documented procurement process.\",\"Offer legitimate commercial discounts where justified.\",\"Escalate the concern to the client\'s appropriate senior authority or compliance function.\",\"Seek legal advice.\",\"Withdraw if the client insists on improper conduct.\",\"The objective is to distinguish a legitimate commercial negotiation from an unethical demand.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and how would you protect the company and its employees?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and how would you protect the company and its employees?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"A responsible approach would include:\",\"Documenting the communication factually.\",\"Preserving relevant records.\",\"Consulting legal and compliance professionals.\",\"Communicating a clear position to the client.\",\"Preventing unauthorised payments.\",\"Protecting employees who raise concerns.\",\"Reviewing internal anti-bribery controls.\",\"A CEO must consider not only whether the company can win a contract, but also how it wins that contract.\"],\"reference_example\":\"A responsible approach would include:\\nDocumenting the communication factually.\\nPreserving relevant records.\\nConsulting legal and compliance professionals.\\nCommunicating a clear position to the client.\\nPreventing unauthorised payments.\\nProtecting employees who raise concerns.\\nReviewing internal anti-bribery controls.\\nA CEO must consider not only whether the company can win a contract, but also how it wins that contract.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"A commercially attractive opportunity is not worth pursuing when its success depends on compromising fundamental ethical or legal standards.\",\"reference_example\":\"A commercially attractive opportunity is not worth pursuing when its success depends on compromising fundamental ethical or legal standards.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"If the same arrangement became public tomorrow, would you be comfortable defending the decision to your employees, customers and stakeholders?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE `title` = 'The Client Who Wants You to Compromise Your Standards', `domain` = 'Entrepreneurship / Business Ethics / Client Management', `primary_trap` = 'Sunk Cost Fallacy', `secondary_trap` = 'Validation Seeking, Catastrophizing, Rationalisation', `content_bundle` = '{\"day\":49,\"phase\":3,\"title\":\"The Client Who Wants You to Compromise Your Standards\",\"domain\":\"Entrepreneurship / Business Ethics / Client Management\",\"mission\":\"Short-term commercial gains should not require compromising the principles on which your business depends.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Recognise ethical pressure in commercial relationships, evaluate reputational exposure and make decisions when revenue conflicts with professional standards.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"6-8\",\"primary_skill\":\"Evaluate\",\"primary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Validation Seeking, Catastrophizing, Rationalisation\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Validation Seeking\",\"Catastrophizing\",\"Rationalisation\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate to high guidance; strategic leadership, financial risk and long-term consequences.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You run a professional consulting firm that has recently secured an opportunity to work with a large corporate client.\\nThe contract could generate ₹1.5 crore in annual revenue and provide access to several future business opportunities.\\nDuring contract discussions, the client\'s procurement head privately suggests that a personal commission would help ensure your company\'s selection and smooth approval of future invoices.\\nHe indicates that similar arrangements are common in the industry.\\nYour sales director recommends accepting the arrangement indirectly through a third-party consultant.\\nHe argues that losing the opportunity would put the company at a disadvantage against competitors.\\nYour finance head is uncomfortable because the proposed payment cannot be justified by any legitimate service.\\nYou have already invested considerable time and money in securing this client.\\nWalking away could affect the company\'s growth targets and employee confidence.\\nYou must decide whether to proceed, challenge the demand, restructure the relationship or withdraw from the opportunity.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"What are the confirmed facts, and what are you assuming about the commercial consequences of refusing the demand?\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. Assumptions explain what the mind projects or fears.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the confirmed facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"assumptions\",\"prompt\":\"Write what you are assuming about this situation.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"The proposed contract is commercially significant.\",\"A personal commission has been suggested.\",\"No legitimate service justifies the proposed payment.\",\"Internal stakeholders disagree about the response.\",\"The company has already invested resources in securing the contract.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"The payment is necessary to secure the contract.\",\"Competitors will accept the same arrangement.\",\"Refusing the demand will permanently close the opportunity.\",\"Using an intermediary will remove responsibility from your company.\",\"The commercial attractiveness of an opportunity does not establish the legitimacy of the means used to secure it.\"]},\"reference_example\":\"Confirmed facts: The proposed contract is commercially significant.; A personal commission has been suggested.; No legitimate service justifies the proposed payment.\\nAssumptions: The payment is necessary to secure the contract.; Competitors will accept the same arrangement.; Refusing the demand will permanently close the opportunity.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"primary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Validation Seeking\",\"Catastrophizing\",\"Rationalisation\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"validation_seeking\",\"catastrophizing\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Sunk Cost Fallacy\\nThe company may feel compelled to accept the demand because of the time and resources already invested in winning the contract.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nSocial Validation Seeking: Justifying the conduct because it is supposedly common in the industry.\\nCatastrophizing: Believing that refusal will seriously threaten the business.\\nRationalisation: Reinterpreting an improper payment as an ordinary commercial expense.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What legal, financial and reputational risks should be evaluated before proceeding?\\n• What information would help distinguish a legitimate commercial arrangement from an improper personal benefit?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What legal, financial and reputational risks should be evaluated before proceeding?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What information would help distinguish a legitimate commercial arrangement from an improper personal benefit?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Relevant considerations include:\",\"Applicable anti-corruption laws.\",\"Company policies and procurement requirements.\",\"Whether a legitimate service is being provided.\",\"Beneficial ownership of intermediaries.\",\"Accounting and tax treatment.\",\"Potential reputational damage.\",\"Contractual and regulatory exposure.\",\"The possibility of reporting the demand through appropriate channels.\",\"The use of an intermediary does not automatically remove the company\'s legal or ethical responsibility.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Relevant considerations include:\",\"Applicable anti-corruption laws.\",\"Company policies and procurement requirements.\",\"Whether a legitimate service is being provided.\",\"Beneficial ownership of intermediaries.\",\"Accounting and tax treatment.\",\"Potential reputational damage.\",\"Contractual and regulatory exposure.\",\"The possibility of reporting the demand through appropriate channels.\",\"The use of an intermediary does not automatically remove the company\'s legal or ethical responsibility.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What alternatives exist beyond accepting the payment demand or immediately abandoning all commercial discussions?\\n• How could you protect the business opportunity while maintaining ethical standards?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What alternatives exist beyond accepting the payment demand or immediately abandoning all commercial discussions?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you protect the business opportunity while maintaining ethical standards?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Reject the personal payment demand.\",\"Request a transparent and documented procurement process.\",\"Offer legitimate commercial discounts where justified.\",\"Escalate the concern to the client\'s appropriate senior authority or compliance function.\",\"Seek legal advice.\",\"Withdraw if the client insists on improper conduct.\",\"The objective is to distinguish a legitimate commercial negotiation from an unethical demand.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Reject the personal payment demand.\",\"Request a transparent and documented procurement process.\",\"Offer legitimate commercial discounts where justified.\",\"Escalate the concern to the client\'s appropriate senior authority or compliance function.\",\"Seek legal advice.\",\"Withdraw if the client insists on improper conduct.\",\"The objective is to distinguish a legitimate commercial negotiation from an unethical demand.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and how would you protect the company and its employees?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next, and how would you protect the company and its employees?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"A responsible approach would include:\",\"Documenting the communication factually.\",\"Preserving relevant records.\",\"Consulting legal and compliance professionals.\",\"Communicating a clear position to the client.\",\"Preventing unauthorised payments.\",\"Protecting employees who raise concerns.\",\"Reviewing internal anti-bribery controls.\",\"A CEO must consider not only whether the company can win a contract, but also how it wins that contract.\"],\"reference_example\":\"A responsible approach would include:\\nDocumenting the communication factually.\\nPreserving relevant records.\\nConsulting legal and compliance professionals.\\nCommunicating a clear position to the client.\\nPreventing unauthorised payments.\\nProtecting employees who raise concerns.\\nReviewing internal anti-bribery controls.\\nA CEO must consider not only whether the company can win a contract, but also how it wins that contract.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"A commercially attractive opportunity is not worth pursuing when its success depends on compromising fundamental ethical or legal standards.\",\"reference_example\":\"A commercially attractive opportunity is not worth pursuing when its success depends on compromising fundamental ethical or legal standards.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"If the same arrangement became public tomorrow, would you be comfortable defending the decision to your employees, customers and stakeholders?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (50, 3, 'The Employee Who Reports a Problem You Did Not Want to Hear', 'Workplace / Whistleblowing / Organisational Accountability', 'Emotional Reasoning', 'Mind Reading, Confirmation Bias, Catastrophizing', '{\"day\":50,\"phase\":3,\"title\":\"The Employee Who Reports a Problem You Did Not Want to Hear\",\"domain\":\"Workplace / Whistleblowing / Organisational Accountability\",\"mission\":\"A leader\'s response to uncomfortable information determines whether the organisation learns or hides its problems.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Recognise defensive leadership, distinguish criticism from disloyalty and establish a culture in which uncomfortable information can be raised safely.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"6-8\",\"primary_skill\":\"Evaluate\",\"primary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Mind Reading, Confirmation Bias, Catastrophizing\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Mind Reading\",\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Catastrophizing\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate to high guidance; strategic leadership, financial risk and long-term consequences.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You are the head of a growing organisation.\\nAn employee from the operations department sends a detailed email to senior management highlighting recurring problems in a major business process.\\nThe email suggests that:\\nManagement reports have been presenting incomplete information.\\nSome operational failures have been repeatedly ignored.\\nEmployees have raised the same concerns earlier.\\nSenior managers were aware of the problems but did not escalate them.\\nThe report indirectly questions decisions taken by you and two senior executives.\\nOne executive believes the employee is attempting to damage management\'s reputation.\\nAnother suggests taking disciplinary action because the employee bypassed the reporting hierarchy.\\nYou are personally uncomfortable because the allegations involve decisions you approved.\\nHowever, you also recognise that some of the reported problems may be genuine.\\nYou must decide whether to defend the management team, investigate the allegations, address the employee\'s conduct or reconsider the underlying systems.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"What are the confirmed facts, and what are you assuming about the employee\'s intentions?\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. Assumptions explain what the mind projects or fears.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the confirmed facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"assumptions\",\"prompt\":\"Write what you are assuming about this situation.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"An employee has raised concerns about operational processes.\",\"The allegations involve senior management decisions.\",\"Some issues may have been raised previously.\",\"Senior executives have different views about the appropriate response.\",\"The concerns have not yet been independently investigated.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"The employee intends to undermine management.\",\"Criticism of management decisions is an act of disloyalty.\",\"The allegations are exaggerated.\",\"Investigating the concerns will damage leadership credibility.\",\"The employee\'s motives and the accuracy of the allegations are separate questions.\"]},\"reference_example\":\"Confirmed facts: An employee has raised concerns about operational processes.; The allegations involve senior management decisions.; Some issues may have been raised previously.\\nAssumptions: The employee intends to undermine management.; Criticism of management decisions is an act of disloyalty.; The allegations are exaggerated.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"primary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Mind Reading\",\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Catastrophizing\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"mind_reading\",\"confirmation_bias\",\"catastrophizing\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Emotional Reasoning\\nManagement may interpret discomfort or embarrassment as evidence that the employee\'s criticism is unfair or inappropriate.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nMind Reading: Assuming the employee\'s intention is to damage management.\\nConfirmation Bias: Looking for evidence that supports the existing management position.\\nCatastrophizing: Believing that acknowledging a problem will destroy organisational confidence.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What evidence would help establish whether the employee\'s allegations are accurate?\\n• What should be examined independently of the employee\'s communication style or reporting approach?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What evidence would help establish whether the employee\'s allegations are accurate?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What should be examined independently of the employee\'s communication style or reporting approach?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Operational records and performance reports.\",\"Earlier complaints and escalation records.\",\"Audit findings.\",\"Process documentation.\",\"Actual versus reported performance.\",\"Relevant management approvals.\",\"Witness accounts.\",\"Whether employees faced pressure not to report problems.\",\"A poorly communicated concern can still contain important information.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Operational records and performance reports.\",\"Earlier complaints and escalation records.\",\"Audit findings.\",\"Process documentation.\",\"Actual versus reported performance.\",\"Relevant management approvals.\",\"Witness accounts.\",\"Whether employees faced pressure not to report problems.\",\"A poorly communicated concern can still contain important information.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What alternatives exist beyond defending management or immediately accepting every allegation?\\n• How could you investigate the matter while protecting both organisational fairness and management accountability?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What alternatives exist beyond defending management or immediately accepting every allegation?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you investigate the matter while protecting both organisational fairness and management accountability?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Commission an independent review.\",\"Establish a confidential investigation process.\",\"Invite the employee to provide supporting information.\",\"Review the existing escalation mechanism.\",\"Separate possible misconduct from legitimate operational concerns.\",\"Introduce stronger reporting and audit controls.\",\"The organisation should investigate facts before assigning motives or blame.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Commission an independent review.\",\"Establish a confidential investigation process.\",\"Invite the employee to provide supporting information.\",\"Review the existing escalation mechanism.\",\"Separate possible misconduct from legitimate operational concerns.\",\"Introduce stronger reporting and audit controls.\",\"The organisation should investigate facts before assigning motives or blame.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do immediately, and how would you communicate your response to the organisation?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do immediately, and how would you communicate your response to the organisation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"A responsible approach would include:\",\"Acknowledging receipt of the concerns.\",\"Preventing retaliation against the employee.\",\"Appointing an appropriately independent investigator.\",\"Preserving relevant documents.\",\"Establishing clear timelines.\",\"Correcting confirmed failures.\",\"Communicating appropriate findings and actions.\",\"A leader\'s credibility is strengthened by responsible accountability, not by pretending that mistakes never occur.\"],\"reference_example\":\"A responsible approach would include:\\nAcknowledging receipt of the concerns.\\nPreventing retaliation against the employee.\\nAppointing an appropriately independent investigator.\\nPreserving relevant documents.\\nEstablishing clear timelines.\\nCorrecting confirmed failures.\\nCommunicating appropriate findings and actions.\\nA leader\'s credibility is strengthened by responsible accountability, not by pretending that mistakes never occur.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"An organisation becomes stronger when leaders are willing to examine information that challenges their own decisions.\",\"reference_example\":\"An organisation becomes stronger when leaders are willing to examine information that challenges their own decisions.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Would you rather lead an organisation where employees tell you what you want to hear or one where they tell you what you need to know?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE `title` = 'The Employee Who Reports a Problem You Did Not Want to Hear', `domain` = 'Workplace / Whistleblowing / Organisational Accountability', `primary_trap` = 'Emotional Reasoning', `secondary_trap` = 'Mind Reading, Confirmation Bias, Catastrophizing', `content_bundle` = '{\"day\":50,\"phase\":3,\"title\":\"The Employee Who Reports a Problem You Did Not Want to Hear\",\"domain\":\"Workplace / Whistleblowing / Organisational Accountability\",\"mission\":\"A leader\'s response to uncomfortable information determines whether the organisation learns or hides its problems.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Recognise defensive leadership, distinguish criticism from disloyalty and establish a culture in which uncomfortable information can be raised safely.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"6-8\",\"primary_skill\":\"Evaluate\",\"primary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Mind Reading, Confirmation Bias, Catastrophizing\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Mind Reading\",\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Catastrophizing\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate to high guidance; strategic leadership, financial risk and long-term consequences.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You are the head of a growing organisation.\\nAn employee from the operations department sends a detailed email to senior management highlighting recurring problems in a major business process.\\nThe email suggests that:\\nManagement reports have been presenting incomplete information.\\nSome operational failures have been repeatedly ignored.\\nEmployees have raised the same concerns earlier.\\nSenior managers were aware of the problems but did not escalate them.\\nThe report indirectly questions decisions taken by you and two senior executives.\\nOne executive believes the employee is attempting to damage management\'s reputation.\\nAnother suggests taking disciplinary action because the employee bypassed the reporting hierarchy.\\nYou are personally uncomfortable because the allegations involve decisions you approved.\\nHowever, you also recognise that some of the reported problems may be genuine.\\nYou must decide whether to defend the management team, investigate the allegations, address the employee\'s conduct or reconsider the underlying systems.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"What are the confirmed facts, and what are you assuming about the employee\'s intentions?\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. Assumptions explain what the mind projects or fears.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the confirmed facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"assumptions\",\"prompt\":\"Write what you are assuming about this situation.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"An employee has raised concerns about operational processes.\",\"The allegations involve senior management decisions.\",\"Some issues may have been raised previously.\",\"Senior executives have different views about the appropriate response.\",\"The concerns have not yet been independently investigated.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"The employee intends to undermine management.\",\"Criticism of management decisions is an act of disloyalty.\",\"The allegations are exaggerated.\",\"Investigating the concerns will damage leadership credibility.\",\"The employee\'s motives and the accuracy of the allegations are separate questions.\"]},\"reference_example\":\"Confirmed facts: An employee has raised concerns about operational processes.; The allegations involve senior management decisions.; Some issues may have been raised previously.\\nAssumptions: The employee intends to undermine management.; Criticism of management decisions is an act of disloyalty.; The allegations are exaggerated.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"primary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Mind Reading\",\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Catastrophizing\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"mind_reading\",\"confirmation_bias\",\"catastrophizing\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Emotional Reasoning\\nManagement may interpret discomfort or embarrassment as evidence that the employee\'s criticism is unfair or inappropriate.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nMind Reading: Assuming the employee\'s intention is to damage management.\\nConfirmation Bias: Looking for evidence that supports the existing management position.\\nCatastrophizing: Believing that acknowledging a problem will destroy organisational confidence.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What evidence would help establish whether the employee\'s allegations are accurate?\\n• What should be examined independently of the employee\'s communication style or reporting approach?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What evidence would help establish whether the employee\'s allegations are accurate?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What should be examined independently of the employee\'s communication style or reporting approach?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Operational records and performance reports.\",\"Earlier complaints and escalation records.\",\"Audit findings.\",\"Process documentation.\",\"Actual versus reported performance.\",\"Relevant management approvals.\",\"Witness accounts.\",\"Whether employees faced pressure not to report problems.\",\"A poorly communicated concern can still contain important information.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Operational records and performance reports.\",\"Earlier complaints and escalation records.\",\"Audit findings.\",\"Process documentation.\",\"Actual versus reported performance.\",\"Relevant management approvals.\",\"Witness accounts.\",\"Whether employees faced pressure not to report problems.\",\"A poorly communicated concern can still contain important information.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What alternatives exist beyond defending management or immediately accepting every allegation?\\n• How could you investigate the matter while protecting both organisational fairness and management accountability?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What alternatives exist beyond defending management or immediately accepting every allegation?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you investigate the matter while protecting both organisational fairness and management accountability?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Commission an independent review.\",\"Establish a confidential investigation process.\",\"Invite the employee to provide supporting information.\",\"Review the existing escalation mechanism.\",\"Separate possible misconduct from legitimate operational concerns.\",\"Introduce stronger reporting and audit controls.\",\"The organisation should investigate facts before assigning motives or blame.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Commission an independent review.\",\"Establish a confidential investigation process.\",\"Invite the employee to provide supporting information.\",\"Review the existing escalation mechanism.\",\"Separate possible misconduct from legitimate operational concerns.\",\"Introduce stronger reporting and audit controls.\",\"The organisation should investigate facts before assigning motives or blame.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do immediately, and how would you communicate your response to the organisation?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do immediately, and how would you communicate your response to the organisation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"A responsible approach would include:\",\"Acknowledging receipt of the concerns.\",\"Preventing retaliation against the employee.\",\"Appointing an appropriately independent investigator.\",\"Preserving relevant documents.\",\"Establishing clear timelines.\",\"Correcting confirmed failures.\",\"Communicating appropriate findings and actions.\",\"A leader\'s credibility is strengthened by responsible accountability, not by pretending that mistakes never occur.\"],\"reference_example\":\"A responsible approach would include:\\nAcknowledging receipt of the concerns.\\nPreventing retaliation against the employee.\\nAppointing an appropriately independent investigator.\\nPreserving relevant documents.\\nEstablishing clear timelines.\\nCorrecting confirmed failures.\\nCommunicating appropriate findings and actions.\\nA leader\'s credibility is strengthened by responsible accountability, not by pretending that mistakes never occur.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"An organisation becomes stronger when leaders are willing to examine information that challenges their own decisions.\",\"reference_example\":\"An organisation becomes stronger when leaders are willing to examine information that challenges their own decisions.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Would you rather lead an organisation where employees tell you what you want to hear or one where they tell you what you need to know?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (51, 3, 'The Promotion That Requires You to Leave a Team You Built', 'Workplace / Career Decisions / Leadership', 'Emotional Reasoning', 'Catastrophizing, Validation Seeking, Sunk Cost Fallacy', '{\"day\":51,\"phase\":3,\"title\":\"The Promotion That Requires You to Leave a Team You Built\",\"domain\":\"Workplace / Career Decisions / Leadership\",\"mission\":\"Career advancement requires evaluating responsibility, personal growth and the cost of staying comfortable.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Evaluate competing career opportunities, separate loyalty from obligation and make decisions based on long-term professional direction.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"6-8\",\"primary_skill\":\"Evaluate\",\"primary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Catastrophizing, Validation Seeking, Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Catastrophizing\",\"Validation Seeking\",\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate to high guidance; strategic leadership, financial risk and long-term consequences.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You have worked in an organisation for eight years.\\nYou joined as a middle-level manager and gradually built a high-performing team.\\nYour current department consistently achieves its targets. Your employees trust you, and senior management considers you an important contributor.\\nYou are now offered a promotion to lead a much larger business unit in another city.\\nThe opportunity includes:\\nHigher compensation.\\nGreater decision-making authority.\\nExposure to senior leadership.\\nResponsibility for a significantly larger team.\\nRelocation and substantial personal adjustments.\\nYour current team is concerned about losing you. Some employees believe the department\'s performance may deteriorate after your departure.\\nYour present manager has also suggested that you should stay for another year because the organisation is going through an important transition.\\nYou feel proud of the team you have built and uncomfortable about leaving at a critical time.\\nHowever, you recognise that rejecting the opportunity could delay your career progression.\\nYou must decide whether to accept the promotion, negotiate the transition or remain in your current position.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"What are the confirmed facts, and what are you assuming about your responsibility towards your current team?\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. Assumptions explain what the mind projects or fears.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the confirmed facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"assumptions\",\"prompt\":\"Write what you are assuming about this situation.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"You have eight years of organisational experience.\",\"Your current team performs well.\",\"A larger leadership opportunity has been offered.\",\"Relocation is required.\",\"Your current manager and team would prefer you to stay.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"Your team cannot succeed without you.\",\"Leaving will be viewed as disloyal.\",\"Rejecting the promotion will improve the department\'s stability.\",\"The opportunity will remain available later.\"]},\"reference_example\":\"Confirmed facts: You have eight years of organisational experience.; Your current team performs well.; A larger leadership opportunity has been offered.\\nAssumptions: Your team cannot succeed without you.; Leaving will be viewed as disloyal.; Rejecting the promotion will improve the department\'s stability.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"primary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Catastrophizing\",\"Validation Seeking\",\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"catastrophizing\",\"validation_seeking\",\"sunk_cost_fallacy\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Emotional Reasoning\\nEmotional attachment to the team may be treated as evidence that leaving is the wrong career decision.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nCatastrophizing: Assuming the team will fail after your departure.\\nValidation Seeking: Prioritising approval from your manager and employees.\\nSunk Cost Fallacy: Feeling obligated to remain because of the years invested in building the department.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What information would help you assess the actual value of the promotion?\\n• How could you determine whether your current team is genuinely dependent on you?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What information would help you assess the actual value of the promotion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you determine whether your current team is genuinely dependent on you?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Responsibilities and authority in the new role.\",\"Long-term career prospects.\",\"Compensation and relocation implications.\",\"Organisational support available in the new position.\",\"Financial and family considerations.\",\"Current team\'s leadership succession readiness.\",\"Availability of capable internal replacements.\",\"Whether your current role offers further growth.\",\"A strong leader should develop people who can eventually operate independently.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Responsibilities and authority in the new role.\",\"Long-term career prospects.\",\"Compensation and relocation implications.\",\"Organisational support available in the new position.\",\"Financial and family considerations.\",\"Current team\'s leadership succession readiness.\",\"Availability of capable internal replacements.\",\"Whether your current role offers further growth.\",\"A strong leader should develop people who can eventually operate independently.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What alternatives exist apart from immediately accepting or rejecting the promotion?\\n• How could you protect your current team\'s stability while pursuing your career opportunity?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What alternatives exist apart from immediately accepting or rejecting the promotion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you protect your current team\'s stability while pursuing your career opportunity?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Accept the promotion with a structured transition plan.\",\"Negotiate a reasonable joining timeline.\",\"Identify and mentor an internal successor.\",\"Offer temporary transition support.\",\"Discuss relocation flexibility.\",\"Explore a comparable internal opportunity without relocation.\",\"Professional growth and responsibility towards a team need not be mutually exclusive.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Accept the promotion with a structured transition plan.\",\"Negotiate a reasonable joining timeline.\",\"Identify and mentor an internal successor.\",\"Offer temporary transition support.\",\"Discuss relocation flexibility.\",\"Explore a comparable internal opportunity without relocation.\",\"Professional growth and responsibility towards a team need not be mutually exclusive.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next before making the decision?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next before making the decision?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Evaluating the new role\'s actual authority and responsibilities.\",\"Discussing personal and family implications.\",\"Clarifying expectations with senior management.\",\"Identifying a successor.\",\"Preparing a transition plan.\",\"Setting a realistic decision deadline.\",\"Do not reject an important opportunity solely because others are comfortable with your continued availability.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Evaluating the new role\'s actual authority and responsibilities.\\nDiscussing personal and family implications.\\nClarifying expectations with senior management.\\nIdentifying a successor.\\nPreparing a transition plan.\\nSetting a realistic decision deadline.\\nDo not reject an important opportunity solely because others are comfortable with your continued availability.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Leadership includes building teams that can function without you and recognising when personal growth requires moving beyond your current responsibilities.\",\"reference_example\":\"Leadership includes building teams that can function without you and recognising when personal growth requires moving beyond your current responsibilities.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"If you have developed a team that cannot function without you, have you succeeded in leadership or created dependency?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
