ion means:\\n• What information would help you assess the actual value of the promotion?\\n• How could you determine whether your current team is genuinely dependent on you?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What information would help you assess the actual value of the promotion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you determine whether your current team is genuinely dependent on you?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Responsibilities and authority in the new role.\",\"Long-term career prospects.\",\"Compensation and relocation implications.\",\"Organisational support available in the new position.\",\"Financial and family considerations.\",\"Current team\'s leadership succession readiness.\",\"Availability of capable internal replacements.\",\"Whether your current role offers further growth.\",\"A strong leader should develop people who can eventually operate independently.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Responsibilities and authority in the new role.\",\"Long-term career prospects.\",\"Compensation and relocation implications.\",\"Organisational support available in the new position.\",\"Financial and family considerations.\",\"Current team\'s leadership succession readiness.\",\"Availability of capable internal replacements.\",\"Whether your current role offers further growth.\",\"A strong leader should develop people who can eventually operate independently.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What alternatives exist apart from immediately accepting or rejecting the promotion?\\n• How could you protect your current team\'s stability while pursuing your career opportunity?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What alternatives exist apart from immediately accepting or rejecting the promotion?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you protect your current team\'s stability while pursuing your career opportunity?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Accept the promotion with a structured transition plan.\",\"Negotiate a reasonable joining timeline.\",\"Identify and mentor an internal successor.\",\"Offer temporary transition support.\",\"Discuss relocation flexibility.\",\"Explore a comparable internal opportunity without relocation.\",\"Professional growth and responsibility towards a team need not be mutually exclusive.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Accept the promotion with a structured transition plan.\",\"Negotiate a reasonable joining timeline.\",\"Identify and mentor an internal successor.\",\"Offer temporary transition support.\",\"Discuss relocation flexibility.\",\"Explore a comparable internal opportunity without relocation.\",\"Professional growth and responsibility towards a team need not be mutually exclusive.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next before making the decision?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do next before making the decision?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Evaluating the new role\'s actual authority and responsibilities.\",\"Discussing personal and family implications.\",\"Clarifying expectations with senior management.\",\"Identifying a successor.\",\"Preparing a transition plan.\",\"Setting a realistic decision deadline.\",\"Do not reject an important opportunity solely because others are comfortable with your continued availability.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Evaluating the new role\'s actual authority and responsibilities.\\nDiscussing personal and family implications.\\nClarifying expectations with senior management.\\nIdentifying a successor.\\nPreparing a transition plan.\\nSetting a realistic decision deadline.\\nDo not reject an important opportunity solely because others are comfortable with your continued availability.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Leadership includes building teams that can function without you and recognising when personal growth requires moving beyond your current responsibilities.\",\"reference_example\":\"Leadership includes building teams that can function without you and recognising when personal growth requires moving beyond your current responsibilities.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"If you have developed a team that cannot function without you, have you succeeded in leadership or created dependency?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (52, 3, 'The Manager Who Takes Credit for Your Work', 'Workplace / Organisational Politics / Professional Reputation', 'Mind Reading', 'Rumination, Emotional Reasoning, Catastrophizing', '{\"day\":52,\"phase\":3,\"title\":\"The Manager Who Takes Credit for Your Work\",\"domain\":\"Workplace / Organisational Politics / Professional Reputation\",\"mission\":\"Professional contribution must be protected through evidence, communication and constructive action rather than emotional confrontation.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Recognise attribution bias, manage professional conflict and protect credibility without allowing resentment to determine behaviour.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"6-8\",\"primary_skill\":\"Evaluate\",\"primary_trap\":\"Mind Reading\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Rumination, Emotional Reasoning, Catastrophizing\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Rumination\",\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"Catastrophizing\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate to high guidance; strategic leadership, financial risk and long-term consequences.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You are a senior manager in a large organisation.\\nOver the last six months, you have led an important business improvement project.\\nYou developed the implementation plan, coordinated multiple departments and supervised execution.\\nThe project has delivered measurable financial savings and improved customer satisfaction.\\nDuring a recent management review, your reporting manager presented the results to the board and described the project as his own initiative.\\nYour contribution was barely acknowledged.\\nThis is not the first time something similar has happened.\\nA colleague privately tells you that your manager is deliberately taking credit because he sees you as a potential competitor.\\nAnother colleague advises you to confront him publicly during the next review.\\nYou are frustrated but also recognise that the manager controls your performance appraisal and future promotion opportunities.\\nYou must decide whether to address the issue privately, document your contributions, escalate the matter or change your approach to professional visibility.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"What are the confirmed facts, and what are you assuming about your manager\'s intentions?\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. Assumptions explain what the mind projects or fears.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the confirmed facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"assumptions\",\"prompt\":\"Write what you are assuming about this situation.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"You led the implementation of the project.\",\"The project delivered measurable results.\",\"Your manager presented the results without adequately acknowledging your contribution.\",\"Similar concerns have arisen previously.\",\"Your manager influences your appraisal and career progression.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"The manager is deliberately trying to undermine your career.\",\"Public confrontation will correct the situation.\",\"Senior management is unaware of your contribution.\",\"Remaining silent is the only way to protect your position.\"]},\"reference_example\":\"Confirmed facts: You led the implementation of the project.; The project delivered measurable results.; Your manager presented the results without adequately acknowledging your contribution.\\nAssumptions: The manager is deliberately trying to undermine your career.; Public confrontation will correct the situation.; Senior management is unaware of your contribution.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"mind_reading\",\"primary_trap\":\"Mind Reading\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Rumination\",\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"Catastrophizing\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"rumination\",\"emotional_reasoning\",\"catastrophizing\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Mind Reading\\nYou may be assuming deliberate malicious intent without sufficient evidence.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nRumination: Repeatedly replaying the incident and becoming increasingly frustrated.\\nEmotional Reasoning: Treating the feeling of being exploited as proof of deliberate misconduct.\\nCatastrophizing: Assuming your professional future is entirely controlled by this manager.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What evidence would establish your actual contribution to the project?\\n• What information would help determine whether this is an isolated incident or a recurring pattern?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What evidence would establish your actual contribution to the project?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What information would help determine whether this is an isolated incident or a recurring pattern?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Project plans and ownership records.\",\"Meeting minutes and email communications.\",\"Performance reports.\",\"Deliverables completed by each team member.\",\"Previous instances of contribution attribution.\",\"Feedback from other stakeholders.\",\"The organisation\'s performance recognition process.\",\"It is important to distinguish inadequate recognition from deliberate professional sabotage.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Project plans and ownership records.\",\"Meeting minutes and email communications.\",\"Performance reports.\",\"Deliverables completed by each team member.\",\"Previous instances of contribution attribution.\",\"Feedback from other stakeholders.\",\"The organisation\'s performance recognition process.\",\"It is important to distinguish inadequate recognition from deliberate professional sabotage.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What options exist beyond remaining silent or confronting your manager publicly?\\n• How could you improve the visibility of your contribution without creating unnecessary conflict?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What options exist beyond remaining silent or confronting your manager publicly?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you improve the visibility of your contribution without creating unnecessary conflict?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Discuss the matter privately with the manager.\",\"Share project progress and outcomes directly through appropriate forums.\",\"Maintain documented records of deliverables.\",\"Request formal project ownership recognition.\",\"Seek feedback from relevant senior stakeholders.\",\"Escalate recurring concerns through appropriate channels.\",\"Explore internal mobility if the environment remains unhealthy.\",\"Professional visibility should be built through evidence and consistent communication.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Discuss the matter privately with the manager.\",\"Share project progress and outcomes directly through appropriate forums.\",\"Maintain documented records of deliverables.\",\"Request formal project ownership recognition.\",\"Seek feedback from relevant senior stakeholders.\",\"Escalate recurring concerns through appropriate channels.\",\"Explore internal mobility if the environment remains unhealthy.\",\"Professional visibility should be built through evidence and consistent communication.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do before the next management review?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do before the next management review?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"A constructive approach would include:\",\"Preparing a factual project contribution summary.\",\"Arranging a private discussion.\",\"Explaining the recognition gap without making unsupported accusations.\",\"Requesting clarity on future project ownership and presentation responsibilities.\",\"Continuing to document measurable achievements.\",\"Reviewing the response and identifying further action if the pattern continues.\",\"Protect your professional credibility without allowing resentment to drive impulsive behaviour.\"],\"reference_example\":\"A constructive approach would include:\\nPreparing a factual project contribution summary.\\nArranging a private discussion.\\nExplaining the recognition gap without making unsupported accusations.\\nRequesting clarity on future project ownership and presentation responsibilities.\\nContinuing to document measurable achievements.\\nReviewing the response and identifying further action if the pattern continues.\\nProtect your professional credibility without allowing resentment to drive impulsive behaviour.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Professional recognition should be supported by evidence, clear communication and consistent ownership of responsibilities.\",\"reference_example\":\"Professional recognition should be supported by evidence, clear communication and consistent ownership of responsibilities.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Are you managing your professional reputation proactively, or expecting others to recognise your contribution automatically?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
