n means:\\n• What evidence would establish your actual contribution to the project?\\n• What information would help determine whether this is an isolated incident or a recurring pattern?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What evidence would establish your actual contribution to the project?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What information would help determine whether this is an isolated incident or a recurring pattern?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Project plans and ownership records.\",\"Meeting minutes and email communications.\",\"Performance reports.\",\"Deliverables completed by each team member.\",\"Previous instances of contribution attribution.\",\"Feedback from other stakeholders.\",\"The organisation\'s performance recognition process.\",\"It is important to distinguish inadequate recognition from deliberate professional sabotage.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Project plans and ownership records.\",\"Meeting minutes and email communications.\",\"Performance reports.\",\"Deliverables completed by each team member.\",\"Previous instances of contribution attribution.\",\"Feedback from other stakeholders.\",\"The organisation\'s performance recognition process.\",\"It is important to distinguish inadequate recognition from deliberate professional sabotage.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What options exist beyond remaining silent or confronting your manager publicly?\\n• How could you improve the visibility of your contribution without creating unnecessary conflict?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What options exist beyond remaining silent or confronting your manager publicly?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you improve the visibility of your contribution without creating unnecessary conflict?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Discuss the matter privately with the manager.\",\"Share project progress and outcomes directly through appropriate forums.\",\"Maintain documented records of deliverables.\",\"Request formal project ownership recognition.\",\"Seek feedback from relevant senior stakeholders.\",\"Escalate recurring concerns through appropriate channels.\",\"Explore internal mobility if the environment remains unhealthy.\",\"Professional visibility should be built through evidence and consistent communication.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Discuss the matter privately with the manager.\",\"Share project progress and outcomes directly through appropriate forums.\",\"Maintain documented records of deliverables.\",\"Request formal project ownership recognition.\",\"Seek feedback from relevant senior stakeholders.\",\"Escalate recurring concerns through appropriate channels.\",\"Explore internal mobility if the environment remains unhealthy.\",\"Professional visibility should be built through evidence and consistent communication.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do before the next management review?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do before the next management review?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"A constructive approach would include:\",\"Preparing a factual project contribution summary.\",\"Arranging a private discussion.\",\"Explaining the recognition gap without making unsupported accusations.\",\"Requesting clarity on future project ownership and presentation responsibilities.\",\"Continuing to document measurable achievements.\",\"Reviewing the response and identifying further action if the pattern continues.\",\"Protect your professional credibility without allowing resentment to drive impulsive behaviour.\"],\"reference_example\":\"A constructive approach would include:\\nPreparing a factual project contribution summary.\\nArranging a private discussion.\\nExplaining the recognition gap without making unsupported accusations.\\nRequesting clarity on future project ownership and presentation responsibilities.\\nContinuing to document measurable achievements.\\nReviewing the response and identifying further action if the pattern continues.\\nProtect your professional credibility without allowing resentment to drive impulsive behaviour.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Professional recognition should be supported by evidence, clear communication and consistent ownership of responsibilities.\",\"reference_example\":\"Professional recognition should be supported by evidence, clear communication and consistent ownership of responsibilities.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Are you managing your professional reputation proactively, or expecting others to recognise your contribution automatically?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (53, 3, 'The Business That Is Growing but Not Making Money', 'Entrepreneurship / Financial Management / Business Model', 'Confirmation Bias', 'Fortune Telling, Validation Seeking, Sunk Cost Fallacy', '{\"day\":53,\"phase\":3,\"title\":\"The Business That Is Growing but Not Making Money\",\"domain\":\"Entrepreneurship / Financial Management / Business Model\",\"mission\":\"Revenue growth can create the illusion of success while the underlying business becomes financially weaker.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Distinguish revenue growth from profitability, identify structural financial weaknesses and evaluate whether a business model needs correction.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"6-8\",\"primary_skill\":\"Evaluate\",\"primary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Fortune Telling, Validation Seeking, Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Fortune Telling\",\"Validation Seeking\",\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate to high guidance; strategic leadership, financial risk and long-term consequences.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You founded a technology-enabled services business four years ago.\\nThe company has grown rapidly.\\nMonthly revenue has increased from ₹8 lakh to ₹45 lakh, and the customer base has expanded significantly.\\nYour investors are pleased with the growth figures.\\nHowever, the business has not generated consistent operating profits.\\nThe reasons include:\\nHigh customer acquisition costs.\\nFrequent discounting to win new customers.\\nRising employee costs.\\nHigh customer servicing expenses.\\nDelayed collections.\\nLow renewal rates among some customer segments.\\nYour sales head argues that profitability will improve once the company achieves greater scale.\\nYour finance head believes the current business model is structurally weak and recommends stopping certain low-margin activities.\\nYour investors want further expansion.\\nYou must decide whether to continue pursuing growth, change pricing, discontinue unprofitable services or slow expansion to improve financial sustainability.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"What are the confirmed facts, and what are you assuming about the relationship between growth and future profitability?\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. Assumptions explain what the mind projects or fears.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the confirmed facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"assumptions\",\"prompt\":\"Write what you are assuming about this situation.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"Revenue has grown substantially.\",\"The business has expanded its customer base.\",\"Operating profitability remains inconsistent.\",\"Customer acquisition and servicing costs are high.\",\"Collection delays are affecting cash flow.\",\"Investors expect further growth.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"Higher revenue will automatically produce profitability.\",\"Current losses are temporary.\",\"Customer acquisition costs will decline with scale.\",\"Investors will continue funding the business indefinitely.\",\"Revenue growth is not proof of a sustainable business model.\"]},\"reference_example\":\"Confirmed facts: Revenue has grown substantially.; The business has expanded its customer base.; Operating profitability remains inconsistent.\\nAssumptions: Higher revenue will automatically produce profitability.; Current losses are temporary.; Customer acquisition costs will decline with scale.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"primary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Fortune Telling\",\"Validation Seeking\",\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"fortune_telling\",\"validation_seeking\",\"sunk_cost_fallacy\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Confirmation Bias\\nManagement may focus on impressive revenue growth while selectively overlooking indicators of weak unit economics.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nFortune Telling: Assuming scale will automatically solve profitability problems.\\nValidation Seeking: Prioritising investor approval and market recognition.\\nSunk Cost Fallacy: Continuing an ineffective model because substantial resources have already been invested.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• Which financial metrics would help determine whether the business is becoming more sustainable?\\n• What evidence would establish whether greater scale can realistically improve profitability?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. Which financial metrics would help determine whether the business is becoming more sustainable?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What evidence would establish whether greater scale can realistically improve profitability?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Relevant measures include:\",\"Gross and contribution margins.\",\"Customer acquisition cost.\",\"Customer lifetime value.\",\"Customer retention and renewal rates.\",\"Revenue per employee.\",\"Cost of servicing each customer.\",\"Operating cash flow.\",\"Receivables and collection cycles.\",\"Break-even revenue.\",\"Profitability by product and customer segment.\",\"The company must establish whether additional revenue contributes positively to the business or increases its losses.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Relevant measures include:\",\"Gross and contribution margins.\",\"Customer acquisition cost.\",\"Customer lifetime value.\",\"Customer retention and renewal rates.\",\"Revenue per employee.\",\"Cost of servicing each customer.\",\"Operating cash flow.\",\"Receivables and collection cycles.\",\"Break-even revenue.\",\"Profitability by product and customer segment.\",\"The company must establish whether additional revenue contributes positively to the business or increases its losses.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What alternatives exist beyond continuing the existing growth strategy or shutting down the business?\\n• How could you restructure the business to improve financial performance without unnecessarily destroying growth potential?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What alternatives exist beyond continuing the existing growth strategy or shutting down the business?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you restructure the business to improve financial performance without unnecessarily destroying growth potential?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Increase prices for underpriced services.\",\"Exit structurally unprofitable customer segments.\",\"Introduce minimum contract values.\",\"Reduce customer acquisition spending.\",\"Improve retention and renewals.\",\"Automate expensive processes.\",\"Restructure employee deployment.\",\"Prioritise higher-margin products.\",\"Slow expansion until unit economics improve.\",\"Growth and profitability need not be opposing objectives if the business model is redesigned appropriately.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Increase prices for underpriced services.\",\"Exit structurally unprofitable customer segments.\",\"Introduce minimum contract values.\",\"Reduce customer acquisition spending.\",\"Improve retention and renewals.\",\"Automate expensive processes.\",\"Restructure employee deployment.\",\"Prioritise higher-margin products.\",\"Slow expansion until unit economics improve.\",\"Growth and profitability need not be opposing objectives if the business model is redesigned appropriately.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What changes would you make first, and what financial milestones would guide your next decision?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What changes would you make first, and what financial milestones would guide your next decision?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Preparing product-level profitability reports.\",\"Identifying loss-making customer segments.\",\"Setting contribution margin targets.\",\"Improving collection efficiency.\",\"Reviewing pricing and discount policies.\",\"Establishing a cash runway.\",\"Creating a realistic profitability timeline.\",\"Monitoring progress through monthly financial reviews.\",\"Do not allow revenue targets to replace financial discipline.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Preparing product-level profitability reports.\\nIdentifying loss-making customer segments.\\nSetting contribution margin targets.\\nImproving collection efficiency.\\nReviewing pricing and discount policies.\\nEstablishing a cash runway.\\nCreating a realistic profitability timeline.\\nMonitoring progress through monthly financial reviews.\\nDo not allow revenue targets to replace financial discipline.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Sustainable growth creates economic value. Increasing revenue without improving the underlying economics can make a business larger without making it stronger.\",\"reference_example\":\"Sustainable growth creates economic value. Increasing revenue without improving the underlying economics can make a business larger without making it stronger.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"If your business doubled its revenue next year but also doubled its losses, would you call that progress?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE `title` = 'The Business That Is Growing but Not Making Money', `domain` = 'Entrepreneurship / Financial Management / Business Model', `primary_trap` = 'Confirmation Bias', `secondary_trap` = 'Fortune Telling, Validation Seeking, Sunk Cost Fallacy', `content_bundle` = '{\"day\":53,\"phase\":3,\"title\":\"The Business That Is Growing but Not Making Money\",\"domain\":\"Entrepreneurship / Financial Management / Business Model\",\"mission\":\"Revenue growth can create the illusion of success while the underlying business becomes financially weaker.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Distinguish revenue growth from profitability, identify structural financial weaknesses and evaluate whether a business model needs correction.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"6-8\",\"primary_skill\":\"Evaluate\",\"primary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Fortune Telling, Validation Seeking, Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Fortune Telling\",\"Validation Seeking\",\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate to high guidance; strategic leadership, financial risk and long-term consequences.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You founded a technology-enabled services business four years ago.\\nThe company has grown rapidly.\\nMonthly revenue has increased from ₹8 lakh to ₹45 lakh, and the customer base has expanded significantly.\\nYour investors are pleased with the growth figures.\\nHowever, the business has not generated consistent operating profits.\\nThe reasons include:\\nHigh customer acquisition costs.\\nFrequent discounting to win new customers.\\nRising employee costs.\\nHigh customer servicing expenses.\\nDelayed collections.\\nLow renewal rates among some customer segments.\\nYour sales head argues that profitability will improve once the company achieves greater scale.\\nYour finance head believes the current business model is structurally weak and recommends stopping certain low-margin activities.\\nYour investors want further expansion.\\nYou must decide whether to continue pursuing growth, change pricing, discontinue unprofitable services or slow expansion to improve financial sustainability.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"What are the confirmed facts, and what are you assuming about the relationship between growth and future profitability?\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. Assumptions explain what the mind projects or fears.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the confirmed facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"assumptions\",\"prompt\":\"Write what you are assuming about this situation.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"Revenue has grown substantially.\",\"The business has expanded its customer base.\",\"Operating profitability remains inconsistent.\",\"Customer acquisition and servicing costs are high.\",\"Collection delays are affecting cash flow.\",\"Investors expect further growth.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"Higher revenue will automatically produce profitability.\",\"Current losses are temporary.\",\"Customer acquisition costs will decline with scale.\",\"Investors will continue funding the business indefinitely.\",\"Revenue growth is not proof of a sustainable business model.\"]},\"reference_example\":\"Confirmed facts: Revenue has grown substantially.; The business has expanded its customer base.; Operating profitability remains inconsistent.\\nAssumptions: Higher revenue will automatically produce profitability.; Current losses are temporary.; Customer acquisition costs will decline with scale.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"primary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Fortune Telling\",\"Validation Seeking\",\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"fortune_telling\",\"validation_seeking\",\"sunk_cost_fallacy\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Confirmation Bias\\nManagement may focus on impressive revenue growth while selectively overlooking indicators of weak unit economics.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nFortune Telling: Assuming scale will automatically solve profitability problems.\\nValidation Seeking: Prioritising investor approval and market recognition.\\nSunk Cost Fallacy: Continuing an ineffective model because substantial resources have already been invested.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• Which financial metrics would help determine whether the business is becoming more sustainable?\\n• What evidence would establish whether greater scale can realistically improve profitability?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. Which financial metrics would help determine whether the business is becoming more sustainable?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What evidence would establish whether greater scale can realistically improve profitability?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Relevant measures include:\",\"Gross and contribution margins.\",\"Customer acquisition cost.\",\"Customer lifetime value.\",\"Customer retention and renewal rates.\",\"Revenue per employee.\",\"Cost of servicing each customer.\",\"Operating cash flow.\",\"Receivables and collection cycles.\",\"Break-even revenue.\",\"Profitability by product and customer segment.\",\"The company must establish whether additional revenue contributes positively to the business or increases its losses.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Relevant measures include:\",\"Gross and contribution margins.\",\"Customer acquisition cost.\",\"Customer lifetime value.\",\"Customer retention and renewal rates.\",\"Revenue per employee.\",\"Cost of servicing each customer.\",\"Operating cash flow.\",\"Receivables and collection cycles.\",\"Break-even revenue.\",\"Profitability by product and customer segment.\",\"The company must establish whether additional revenue contributes positively to the business or increases its losses.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What alternatives exist beyond continuing the existing growth strategy or shutting down the business?\\n• How could you restructure the business to improve financial performance without unnecessarily destroying growth potential?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What alternatives exist beyond continuing the existing growth strategy or shutting down the business?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you restructure the business to improve financial performance without unnecessarily destroying growth potential?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Increase prices for underpriced services.\",\"Exit structurally unprofitable customer segments.\",\"Introduce minimum contract values.\",\"Reduce customer acquisition spending.\",\"Improve retention and renewals.\",\"Automate expensive processes.\",\"Restructure employee deployment.\",\"Prioritise higher-margin products.\",\"Slow expansion until unit economics improve.\",\"Growth and profitability need not be opposing objectives if the business model is redesigned appropriately.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Increase prices for underpriced services.\",\"Exit structurally unprofitable customer segments.\",\"Introduce minimum contract values.\",\"Reduce customer acquisition spending.\",\"Improve retention and renewals.\",\"Automate expensive processes.\",\"Restructure employee deployment.\",\"Prioritise higher-margin products.\",\"Slow expansion until unit economics improve.\",\"Growth and profitability need not be opposing objectives if the business model is redesigned appropriately.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What changes would you make first, and what financial milestones would guide your next decision?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What changes would you make first, and what financial milestones would guide your next decision?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Preparing product-level profitability reports.\",\"Identifying loss-making customer segments.\",\"Setting contribution margin targets.\",\"Improving collection efficiency.\",\"Reviewing pricing and discount policies.\",\"Establishing a cash runway.\",\"Creating a realistic profitability timeline.\",\"Monitoring progress through monthly financial reviews.\",\"Do not allow revenue targets to replace financial discipline.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Preparing product-level profitability reports.\\nIdentifying loss-making customer segments.\\nSetting contribution margin targets.\\nImproving collection efficiency.\\nReviewing pricing and discount policies.\\nEstablishing a cash runway.\\nCreating a realistic profitability timeline.\\nMonitoring progress through monthly financial reviews.\\nDo not allow revenue targets to replace financial discipline.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Sustainable growth creates economic value. Increasing revenue without improving the underlying economics can make a business larger without making it stronger.\",\"reference_example\":\"Sustainable growth creates economic value. Increasing revenue without improving the underlying economics can make a business larger without making it stronger.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"If your business doubled its revenue next year but also doubled its losses, would you call that progress?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (54, 3, 'The Employee Who Is Not Performing Despite Repeated Support', 'Workplace / Performance Management', 'Emotional Reasoning', 'Sunk Cost Fallacy, All-or-Nothing Thinking, Catastrophizing', '{\"day\":54,\"phase\":3,\"title\":\"The Employee Who Is Not Performing Despite Repeated Support\",\"domain\":\"Workplace / Performance Management\",\"mission\":\"Compassion in leadership must be balanced with fairness, accountability and organisational requirements.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Separate personal empathy from performance expectations, evaluate capability gaps and make fair decisions about underperformance.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"6-8\",\"primary_skill\":\"Evaluate\",\"primary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy, All-or-Nothing Thinking, Catastrophizing\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"Catastrophizing\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate to high guidance; strategic leadership, financial risk and long-term consequences.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You manage a department of 35 employees.\\nOne of your senior managers has been with the organisation for seven years.\\nThe employee has historically performed well but has struggled over the last 12 months.\\nSeveral targets have been missed, deadlines are regularly extended and team productivity has declined.\\nYou have already:\\nProvided additional training.\\nAssigned a mentor.\\nReduced some responsibilities.\\nConducted multiple counselling sessions.\\nThe employee has also shared personal difficulties affecting concentration and work performance.\\nHR recommends a formal performance improvement plan.\\nOne senior manager believes that terminating the employee would be unfair after seven years of service.\\nAnother believes that continuing to accommodate poor performance is unfair to the rest of the team.\\nYou are concerned about the employee\'s personal circumstances, but the department cannot continue operating below required standards.\\nYou must decide how to balance empathy, support and accountability.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"What are the confirmed facts, and what are you assuming about the employee\'s ability to improve?\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. Assumptions explain what the mind projects or fears.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the confirmed facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"assumptions\",\"prompt\":\"Write what you are assuming about this situation.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"The employee has seven years of service.\",\"Performance has declined over the last 12 months.\",\"Several support measures have already been provided.\",\"Personal difficulties have been reported.\",\"Departmental performance is being affected.\",\"HR has recommended a formal improvement process.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"The employee cannot improve further.\",\"Termination would necessarily be unfair.\",\"Personal circumstances fully explain the performance decline.\",\"Other employees will accept continued underperformance.\"]},\"reference_example\":\"Confirmed facts: The employee has seven years of service.; Performance has declined over the last 12 months.; Several support measures have already been provided.\\nAssumptions: The employee cannot improve further.; Termination would necessarily be unfair.; Personal circumstances fully explain the performance decline.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"primary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"Catastrophizing\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"all_or_nothing\",\"catastrophizing\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Emotional Reasoning\\nThe manager may allow sympathy or guilt to replace objective evaluation of performance and organisational needs.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nSunk Cost Fallacy: Giving disproportionate weight to the employee\'s long service.\\nAll-or-Nothing Thinking: Assuming the only options are indefinite support or termination.\\nCatastrophizing: Believing that taking formal action will inevitably harm the employee.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What evidence would help distinguish a capability problem, a motivation problem and a temporary personal difficulty?\\n• What responsibilities does the organisation have towards the employee and the wider team?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What evidence would help distinguish a capability problem, a motivation problem and a temporary personal difficulty?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What responsibilities does the organisation have towards the employee and the wider team?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Historical performance trends.\",\"Current role requirements.\",\"Quality and timeliness of deliverables.\",\"Training and coaching records.\",\"Feedback from colleagues.\",\"Whether targets are realistic.\",\"Workload and resource availability.\",\"Employee feedback and support requirements.\",\"Applicable employment policies and legal obligations.\",\"Fairness requires considering the employee\'s circumstances without ignoring the impact on others.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Historical performance trends.\",\"Current role requirements.\",\"Quality and timeliness of deliverables.\",\"Training and coaching records.\",\"Feedback from colleagues.\",\"Whether targets are realistic.\",\"Workload and resource availability.\",\"Employee feedback and support requirements.\",\"Applicable employment policies and legal obligations.\",\"Fairness requires considering the employee\'s circumstances without ignoring the impact on others.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What alternatives exist apart from continuing the current arrangement or immediately terminating employment?\\n• How could the role or support structure be redesigned to give the employee a reasonable opportunity to improve?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What alternatives exist apart from continuing the current arrangement or immediately terminating employment?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could the role or support structure be redesigned to give the employee a reasonable opportunity to improve?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Formal performance improvement plan.\",\"Temporary adjustment of responsibilities.\",\"Additional training.\",\"Role reassignment where appropriate.\",\"Defined support and review period.\",\"Mutual separation where suitable.\",\"Formal termination if reasonable support fails and the performance gap remains material.\",\"Compassion does not require eliminating accountability.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Formal performance improvement plan.\",\"Temporary adjustment of responsibilities.\",\"Additional training.\",\"Role reassignment where appropriate.\",\"Defined support and review period.\",\"Mutual separation where suitable.\",\"Formal termination if reasonable support fails and the performance gap remains material.\",\"Compassion does not require eliminating accountability.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you communicate to the employee, and how would you determine whether improvement is sufficient?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What would you communicate to the employee, and how would you determine whether improvement is sufficient?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Conducting a documented performance review.\",\"Clearly communicating expectations.\",\"Understanding the employee\'s concerns.\",\"Defining achievable performance targets.\",\"Providing reasonable support.\",\"Setting review dates.\",\"Following a fair and consistent HR process.\",\"Avoid making employment decisions based solely on frustration or guilt.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Conducting a documented performance review.\\nClearly communicating expectations.\\nUnderstanding the employee\'s concerns.\\nDefining achievable performance targets.\\nProviding reasonable support.\\nSetting review dates.\\nFollowing a fair and consistent HR process.\\nAvoid making employment decisions based solely on frustration or guilt.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Good leadership combines empathy with accountability. Fair treatment means providing appropriate support while maintaining reasonable standards for everyone.\",\"reference_example\":\"Good leadership combines empathy with accountability. Fair treatment means providing appropriate support while maintaining reasonable standards for everyone.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"When does protecting one employee from difficult feedback become unfair to the rest of the team?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE `title` = 'The Employee Who Is Not Performing Despite Repeated Support', `domain` = 'Workplace / Performance Management', `primary_trap` = 'Emotional Reasoning', `secondary_trap` = 'Sunk Cost Fallacy, All-or-Nothing Thinking, Catastrophizing', `content_bundle` = '{\"day\":54,\"phase\":3,\"title\":\"The Employee Who Is Not Performing Despite Repeated Support\",\"domain\":\"Workplace / Performance Management\",\"mission\":\"Compassion in leadership must be balanced with fairness, accountability and organisational requirements.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Separate personal empathy from performance expectations, evaluate capability gaps and make fair decisions about underperformance.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"6-8\",\"primary_skill\":\"Evaluate\",\"primary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy, All-or-Nothing Thinking, Catastrophizing\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"Catastrophizing\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate to high guidance; strategic leadership, financial risk and long-term consequences.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You manage a department of 35 employees.\\nOne of your senior managers has been with the organisation for seven years.\\nThe employee has historically performed well but has struggled over the last 12 months.\\nSeveral targets have been missed, deadlines are regularly extended and team productivity has declined.\\nYou have already:\\nProvided additional training.\\nAssigned a mentor.\\nReduced some responsibilities.\\nConducted multiple counselling sessions.\\nThe employee has also shared personal difficulties affecting concentration and work performance.\\nHR recommends a formal performance improvement plan.\\nOne senior manager believes that terminating the employee would be unfair after seven years of service.\\nAnother believes that continuing to accommodate poor performance is unfair to the rest of the team.\\nYou are concerned about the employee\'s personal circumstances, but the department cannot continue operating below required standards.\\nYou must decide how to balance empathy, support and accountability.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"What are the confirmed facts, and what are you assuming about the employee\'s ability to improve?\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. Assumptions explain what the mind projects or fears.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the confirmed facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"assumptions\",\"prompt\":\"Write what you are assuming about this situation.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"The employee has seven years of service.\",\"Performance has declined over the last 12 months.\",\"Several support measures have already been provided.\",\"Personal difficulties have been reported.\",\"Departmental performance is being affected.\",\"HR has recommended a formal improvement process.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"The employee cannot improve further.\",\"Termination would necessarily be unfair.\",\"Personal circumstances fully explain the performance decline.\",\"Other employees will accept continued underperformance.\"]},\"reference_example\":\"Confirmed facts: The employee has seven years of service.; Performance has declined over the last 12 months.; Several support measures have already been provided.\\nAssumptions: The employee cannot improve further.; Termination would necessarily be unfair.; Personal circumstances fully explain the performance decline.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"f