key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"primary_trap\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"Confirmation Bias\",\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"emotional_reasoning\",\"confirmation_bias\",\"all_or_nothing\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Fortune Telling\\nYou may be assuming that immediate acceptance is necessary because the opportunity may not remain available.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nEmotional Reasoning: Allowing excitement about entrepreneurship to minimise potential conflicts.\\nConfirmation Bias: Focusing on the opportunity while overlooking employment restrictions.\\nAll-or-Nothing Thinking: Assuming you must either accept immediately or abandon entrepreneurship completely.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What legal, contractual and commercial information should you review before proceeding?\\n• Which resources or relationships can you legitimately use, and which must remain with your current employer?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What legal, contractual and commercial information should you review before proceeding?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. Which resources or relationships can you legitimately use, and which must remain with your current employer?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Relevant considerations include:\",\"Employment agreement.\",\"Confidentiality and intellectual property provisions.\",\"Conflict-of-interest policies.\",\"Non-solicitation obligations, where applicable.\",\"Fiduciary duties and applicable law.\",\"Ownership of business plans and work products.\",\"Source of the proposed customer relationships.\",\"Whether the proposed business can operate independently.\",\"Your professional experience is valuable. Your employer\'s confidential information is not yours to transfer.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Relevant considerations include:\",\"Employment agreement.\",\"Confidentiality and intellectual property provisions.\",\"Conflict-of-interest policies.\",\"Non-solicitation obligations, where applicable.\",\"Fiduciary duties and applicable law.\",\"Ownership of business plans and work products.\",\"Source of the proposed customer relationships.\",\"Whether the proposed business can operate independently.\",\"Your professional experience is valuable. Your employer\'s confidential information is not yours to transfer.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What alternatives exist beyond immediately starting the competing business or abandoning the opportunity?\\n• How could you pursue entrepreneurship without creating an avoidable conflict with your current employer?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What alternatives exist beyond immediately starting the competing business or abandoning the opportunity?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you pursue entrepreneurship without creating an avoidable conflict with your current employer?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Negotiate a future joining or investment arrangement.\",\"Obtain appropriate written clearance where possible.\",\"Explore a non-competing business segment.\",\"Develop an independent business plan without using confidential information.\",\"Wait until employment obligations have been properly concluded.\",\"Decline the opportunity if the conflict cannot be responsibly resolved.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Negotiate a future joining or investment arrangement.\",\"Obtain appropriate written clearance where possible.\",\"Explore a non-competing business segment.\",\"Develop an independent business plan without using confidential information.\",\"Wait until employment obligations have been properly concluded.\",\"Decline the opportunity if the conflict cannot be responsibly resolved.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do before signing any agreement with the investor?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do before signing any agreement with the investor?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"A responsible approach would include:\",\"Reviewing all employment obligations.\",\"Seeking independent legal advice.\",\"Disclosing conflicts where required.\",\"Separating personal business development from employer resources.\",\"Avoiding use of confidential information.\",\"Clarifying the investor\'s expectations.\",\"Establishing a legitimate transition plan.\",\"An entrepreneurial opportunity should not depend on the misuse of professional trust.\"],\"reference_example\":\"A responsible approach would include:\\nReviewing all employment obligations.\\nSeeking independent legal advice.\\nDisclosing conflicts where required.\\nSeparating personal business development from employer resources.\\nAvoiding use of confidential information.\\nClarifying the investor\'s expectations.\\nEstablishing a legitimate transition plan.\\nAn entrepreneurial opportunity should not depend on the misuse of professional trust.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Professional ambition and ethical responsibility can coexist. The manner in which you leave one organisation matters as much as the opportunity you pursue next.\",\"reference_example\":\"Professional ambition and ethical responsibility can coexist. The manner in which you leave one organisation matters as much as the opportunity you pursue next.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"Would you be comfortable if your current employer used the same methods against you that you are considering using against them?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (56, 3, 'The Product That You Know Is Failing but Your Investors Still Support', 'Entrepreneurship / Strategic Decision-Making / Product Failure', 'Sunk Cost Fallacy', 'Confirmation Bias, Emotional Reasoning, Validation Seeking', '{\"day\":56,\"phase\":3,\"title\":\"The Product That You Know Is Failing but Your Investors Still Support\",\"domain\":\"Entrepreneurship / Strategic Decision-Making / Product Failure\",\"mission\":\"Leadership requires recognising when persistence has stopped creating value.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Separate commitment from stubbornness, recognise escalation of commitment and evaluate whether to continue, pivot or discontinue an underperforming business initiative.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"6-8\",\"primary_skill\":\"Evaluate\",\"primary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias, Emotional Reasoning, Validation Seeking\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"Validation Seeking\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate to high guidance; strategic leadership, financial risk and long-term consequences.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You founded a technology company five years ago.\\nTwo years ago, you launched a new product after investing ₹2 crore in development and marketing.\\nThe product was expected to become the company\'s primary growth engine.\\nHowever, performance has been disappointing:\\nCustomer adoption is significantly below projections.\\nProduct development costs continue to rise.\\nSeveral customers have discontinued subscriptions.\\nCompetitors offer better functionality at lower prices.\\nThe sales team struggles to explain the product\'s differentiation.\\nYour investors remain supportive because they believe the market opportunity is large.\\nYour product head believes that another ₹75 lakh and six months of development could improve the product.\\nYour finance head recommends discontinuing the initiative before it consumes more capital.\\nYou feel personally attached because you championed the product and persuaded the board to approve the initial investment.\\nYou must decide whether to invest further, pivot, sell the product or discontinue it.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"What are the confirmed facts, and what are you assuming about the product\'s future potential?\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. Assumptions explain what the mind projects or fears.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the confirmed facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"assumptions\",\"prompt\":\"Write what you are assuming about this situation.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"₹2 crore has already been invested.\",\"Customer adoption is below projections.\",\"Development costs continue to increase.\",\"Customer retention is weak.\",\"Competitors offer alternatives.\",\"An additional ₹75 lakh is being proposed.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"Additional investment will solve the adoption problem.\",\"The market opportunity guarantees future demand.\",\"Discontinuing the product means admitting failure.\",\"The original investment must be recovered through continued development.\",\"Past expenditure cannot be recovered simply by spending more.\"]},\"reference_example\":\"Confirmed facts: ₹2 crore has already been invested.; Customer adoption is below projections.; Development costs continue to increase.\\nAssumptions: Additional investment will solve the adoption problem.; The market opportunity guarantees future demand.; Discontinuing the product means admitting failure.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"primary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"Validation Seeking\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"confirmation_bias\",\"emotional_reasoning\",\"validation_seeking\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Sunk Cost Fallacy\\nThe founder may continue investing because of the amount already spent rather than evaluating the next investment independently.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nConfirmation Bias: Highlighting positive customer feedback while ignoring poor adoption.\\nEmotional Reasoning: Treating product discontinuation as a personal failure.\\nValidation Seeking: Continuing partly to protect credibility with investors and the board.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What evidence would establish whether the product still has a commercially viable future?\\n• What would need to be true for the additional ₹75 lakh investment to be justified?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What evidence would establish whether the product still has a commercially viable future?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What would need to be true for the additional ₹75 lakh investment to be justified?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Active paying customers.\",\"Customer retention and churn.\",\"Product usage and adoption.\",\"Customer acquisition cost.\",\"Contribution margin.\",\"Competitor positioning.\",\"Customer feedback and unmet needs.\",\"Development milestones.\",\"Probability of reaching break-even.\",\"Alternative uses of the proposed investment.\",\"The decision must compare the expected future value of continuing with the expected value of pivoting or exiting.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Active paying customers.\",\"Customer retention and churn.\",\"Product usage and adoption.\",\"Customer acquisition cost.\",\"Contribution margin.\",\"Competitor positioning.\",\"Customer feedback and unmet needs.\",\"Development milestones.\",\"Probability of reaching break-even.\",\"Alternative uses of the proposed investment.\",\"The decision must compare the expected future value of continuing with the expected value of pivoting or exiting.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What alternatives exist beyond investing another ₹75 lakh or immediately abandoning the product?\\n• How could you preserve any remaining value while limiting further financial exposure?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What alternatives exist beyond investing another ₹75 lakh or immediately abandoning the product?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you preserve any remaining value while limiting further financial exposure?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Conduct a limited customer-led pilot.\",\"Pivot towards a narrower customer segment.\",\"Reduce the product\'s feature scope.\",\"Partner with an established technology provider.\",\"License the technology.\",\"Sell the product or relevant intellectual property.\",\"Discontinue development and redirect resources.\",\"Persistence is valuable when supported by evidence. It becomes expensive when it prevents objective evaluation.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Conduct a limited customer-led pilot.\",\"Pivot towards a narrower customer segment.\",\"Reduce the product\'s feature scope.\",\"Partner with an established technology provider.\",\"License the technology.\",\"Sell the product or relevant intellectual property.\",\"Discontinue development and redirect resources.\",\"Persistence is valuable when supported by evidence. It becomes expensive when it prevents objective evaluation.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What decision would you present to the board, and what measurable conditions would support it?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What decision would you present to the board, and what measurable conditions would support it?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Independent product and financial review.\",\"Customer interviews.\",\"A revised business case.\",\"A capped pilot budget.\",\"Specific adoption and retention targets.\",\"A clear review deadline.\",\"Defined continuation and exit criteria.\",\"The board should evaluate the next investment on its future merits, not on the amount already committed.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Independent product and financial review.\\nCustomer interviews.\\nA revised business case.\\nA capped pilot budget.\\nSpecific adoption and retention targets.\\nA clear review deadline.\\nDefined continuation and exit criteria.\\nThe board should evaluate the next investment on its future merits, not on the amount already committed.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"A failed initiative is not necessarily a failed entrepreneur. The ability to stop, learn and redirect resources is an essential part of sound business judgment.\",\"reference_example\":\"A failed initiative is not necessarily a failed entrepreneur. The ability to stop, learn and redirect resources is an essential part of sound business judgment.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"If you had not invested ₹2 crore already, would you approve spending another ₹75 lakh today?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE `title` = 'The Product That You Know Is Failing but Your Investors Still Support', `domain` = 'Entrepreneurship / Strategic Decision-Making / Product Failure', `primary_trap` = 'Sunk Cost Fallacy', `secondary_trap` = 'Confirmation Bias, Emotional Reasoning, Validation Seeking', `content_bundle` = '{\"day\":56,\"phase\":3,\"title\":\"The Product That You Know Is Failing but Your Investors Still Support\",\"domain\":\"Entrepreneurship / Strategic Decision-Making / Product Failure\",\"mission\":\"Leadership requires recognising when persistence has stopped creating value.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Separate commitment from stubbornness, recognise escalation of commitment and evaluate whether to continue, pivot or discontinue an underperforming business initiative.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"6-8\",\"primary_skill\":\"Evaluate\",\"primary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Confirmation Bias, Emotional Reasoning, Validation Seeking\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"Validation Seeking\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate to high guidance; strategic leadership, financial risk and long-term consequences.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You founded a technology company five years ago.\\nTwo years ago, you launched a new product after investing ₹2 crore in development and marketing.\\nThe product was expected to become the company\'s primary growth engine.\\nHowever, performance has been disappointing:\\nCustomer adoption is significantly below projections.\\nProduct development costs continue to rise.\\nSeveral customers have discontinued subscriptions.\\nCompetitors offer better functionality at lower prices.\\nThe sales team struggles to explain the product\'s differentiation.\\nYour investors remain supportive because they believe the market opportunity is large.\\nYour product head believes that another ₹75 lakh and six months of development could improve the product.\\nYour finance head recommends discontinuing the initiative before it consumes more capital.\\nYou feel personally attached because you championed the product and persuaded the board to approve the initial investment.\\nYou must decide whether to invest further, pivot, sell the product or discontinue it.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"What are the confirmed facts, and what are you assuming about the product\'s future potential?\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. Assumptions explain what the mind projects or fears.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the confirmed facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"assumptions\",\"prompt\":\"Write what you are assuming about this situation.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"₹2 crore has already been invested.\",\"Customer adoption is below projections.\",\"Development costs continue to increase.\",\"Customer retention is weak.\",\"Competitors offer alternatives.\",\"An additional ₹75 lakh is being proposed.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"Additional investment will solve the adoption problem.\",\"The market opportunity guarantees future demand.\",\"Discontinuing the product means admitting failure.\",\"The original investment must be recovered through continued development.\",\"Past expenditure cannot be recovered simply by spending more.\"]},\"reference_example\":\"Confirmed facts: ₹2 crore has already been invested.; Customer adoption is below projections.; Development costs continue to increase.\\nAssumptions: Additional investment will solve the adoption problem.; The market opportunity guarantees future demand.; Discontinuing the product means admitting failure.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"primary_trap\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"Validation Seeking\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"confirmation_bias\",\"emotional_reasoning\",\"validation_seeking\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Sunk Cost Fallacy\\nThe founder may continue investing because of the amount already spent rather than evaluating the next investment independently.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nConfirmation Bias: Highlighting positive customer feedback while ignoring poor adoption.\\nEmotional Reasoning: Treating product discontinuation as a personal failure.\\nValidation Seeking: Continuing partly to protect credibility with investors and the board.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What evidence would establish whether the product still has a commercially viable future?\\n• What would need to be true for the additional ₹75 lakh investment to be justified?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What evidence would establish whether the product still has a commercially viable future?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. What would need to be true for the additional ₹75 lakh investment to be justified?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Active paying customers.\",\"Customer retention and churn.\",\"Product usage and adoption.\",\"Customer acquisition cost.\",\"Contribution margin.\",\"Competitor positioning.\",\"Customer feedback and unmet needs.\",\"Development milestones.\",\"Probability of reaching break-even.\",\"Alternative uses of the proposed investment.\",\"The decision must compare the expected future value of continuing with the expected value of pivoting or exiting.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Active paying customers.\",\"Customer retention and churn.\",\"Product usage and adoption.\",\"Customer acquisition cost.\",\"Contribution margin.\",\"Competitor positioning.\",\"Customer feedback and unmet needs.\",\"Development milestones.\",\"Probability of reaching break-even.\",\"Alternative uses of the proposed investment.\",\"The decision must compare the expected future value of continuing with the expected value of pivoting or exiting.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What alternatives exist beyond investing another ₹75 lakh or immediately abandoning the product?\\n• How could you preserve any remaining value while limiting further financial exposure?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What alternatives exist beyond investing another ₹75 lakh or immediately abandoning the product?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you preserve any remaining value while limiting further financial exposure?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Conduct a limited customer-led pilot.\",\"Pivot towards a narrower customer segment.\",\"Reduce the product\'s feature scope.\",\"Partner with an established technology provider.\",\"License the technology.\",\"Sell the product or relevant intellectual property.\",\"Discontinue development and redirect resources.\",\"Persistence is valuable when supported by evidence. It becomes expensive when it prevents objective evaluation.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Conduct a limited customer-led pilot.\",\"Pivot towards a narrower customer segment.\",\"Reduce the product\'s feature scope.\",\"Partner with an established technology provider.\",\"License the technology.\",\"Sell the product or relevant intellectual property.\",\"Discontinue development and redirect resources.\",\"Persistence is valuable when supported by evidence. It becomes expensive when it prevents objective evaluation.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What decision would you present to the board, and what measurable conditions would support it?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What decision would you present to the board, and what measurable conditions would support it?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Independent product and financial review.\",\"Customer interviews.\",\"A revised business case.\",\"A capped pilot budget.\",\"Specific adoption and retention targets.\",\"A clear review deadline.\",\"Defined continuation and exit criteria.\",\"The board should evaluate the next investment on its future merits, not on the amount already committed.\"],\"reference_example\":\"Independent product and financial review.\\nCustomer interviews.\\nA revised business case.\\nA capped pilot budget.\\nSpecific adoption and retention targets.\\nA clear review deadline.\\nDefined continuation and exit criteria.\\nThe board should evaluate the next investment on its future merits, not on the amount already committed.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"A failed initiative is not necessarily a failed entrepreneur. The ability to stop, learn and redirect resources is an essential part of sound business judgment.\",\"reference_example\":\"A failed initiative is not necessarily a failed entrepreneur. The ability to stop, learn and redirect resources is an essential part of sound business judgment.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"If you had not invested ₹2 crore already, would you approve spending another ₹75 lakh today?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', `updated_at` = '2026-11-10 12:00:00';

INSERT INTO `foundation_days` (`day_number`, `phase`, `title`, `domain`, `primary_trap`, `secondary_trap`, `content_bundle`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
VALUES (57, 3, 'The Major Client Complaint That Could Damage Your Reputation', 'Entrepreneurship / Crisis Management / Customer Trust', 'Catastrophizing', 'Emotional Reasoning, Confirmation Bias, Fortune Telling', '{\"day\":57,\"phase\":3,\"title\":\"The Major Client Complaint That Could Damage Your Reputation\",\"domain\":\"Entrepreneurship / Crisis Management / Customer Trust\",\"mission\":\"Protecting reputation requires confronting problems early rather than managing appearances.\",\"learning_objective\":\"Respond to reputational threats, distinguish communication from concealment and understand the importance of timely accountability.\",\"difficulty\":\"Advanced\",\"emotional_intensity\":\"High\",\"estimated_minutes\":\"6-8\",\"primary_skill\":\"Evaluate\",\"primary_trap\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"secondary_trap\":\"Emotional Reasoning, Confirmation Bias, Fortune Telling\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Fortune Telling\"],\"guidance_level\":\"Moderate to high guidance; strategic leadership, financial risk and long-term consequences.\",\"interaction_principle\":\"Think → Commit → Compare → Reflect\",\"scenario_text\":\"You are the CEO of a company providing specialised services to institutional customers.\\nA major client has publicly posted a detailed complaint about your organisation.\\nThe complaint alleges:\\nRepeated service failures.\\nPoor communication.\\nUnresolved customer grievances.\\nInadequate management response.\\nThe post is gaining attention on professional social media platforms.\\nYour sales head wants to respond immediately and describe the complaint as exaggerated.\\nYour operations head believes the complaint has some merit and recommends an internal investigation.\\nYour communications consultant advises against making any public admission until the facts are established.\\nMeanwhile, other customers have started asking questions.\\nYou know that some service failures have occurred, but you are not certain whether the specific allegations are entirely accurate.\\nA poorly handled response could affect customer trust and future business.\\nYou must decide how to communicate, investigate and address the situation.\",\"steps\":[{\"step_number\":1,\"key\":\"detect\",\"prompt\":\"What are the confirmed facts, and what are you assuming about the accuracy and impact of the complaint?\",\"insight\":\"Facts describe what is known. Assumptions explain what the mind projects or fears.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"facts\",\"prompt\":\"Write only the confirmed facts.\",\"multiline\":true},{\"field_key\":\"assumptions\",\"prompt\":\"Write what you are assuming about this situation.\",\"multiline\":true}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":{\"facts\":[\"A major customer has published a complaint.\",\"The complaint is receiving public attention.\",\"Some service failures have occurred.\",\"The full allegations have not been independently verified.\",\"Other customers are seeking clarification.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"The complaint is deliberately exaggerated.\",\"A public response will resolve the issue.\",\"Admitting any failure will destroy the company\'s reputation.\",\"Ignoring the complaint will make it disappear.\",\"A public allegation and a verified operational failure are not the same thing. Both require appropriate examination.\"]},\"reference_example\":\"Confirmed facts: A major customer has published a complaint.; The complaint is receiving public attention.; Some service failures have occurred.\\nAssumptions: The complaint is deliberately exaggerated.; A public response will resolve the issue.; Admitting any failure will destroy the company\'s reputation.\"},{\"step_number\":2,\"key\":\"decode\",\"prompt\":\"Which thinking trap(s) may be influencing your judgment, and why?\",\"input_type\":\"single_choice_with_multi_notes\",\"options\":[{\"key\":\"mind_reading\",\"label\":\"Mind Reading\",\"definition\":\"Assuming others\' intentions without evidence.\"},{\"key\":\"fortune_telling\",\"label\":\"Fortune Telling\",\"definition\":\"Treating an unverified prediction as certain.\"},{\"key\":\"emotional_reasoning\",\"label\":\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"definition\":\"Treating a feeling as proof of reality.\"},{\"key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"label\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"definition\":\"Assuming the absolute worst outcome.\"},{\"key\":\"confirmation_bias\",\"label\":\"Confirmation Bias\",\"definition\":\"Only seeing details that confirm the feared story.\"},{\"key\":\"rumination\",\"label\":\"Rumination\",\"definition\":\"Repetitive, circular overthinking of past events.\"},{\"key\":\"all_or_nothing\",\"label\":\"All-or-Nothing Thinking\",\"definition\":\"Treating a minor gap as total failure or framing as either-or.\"},{\"key\":\"validation_seeking\",\"label\":\"Validation Seeking\",\"definition\":\"Allowing external approval to define self-worth or decisions.\"},{\"key\":\"sunk_cost_fallacy\",\"label\":\"Sunk Cost Fallacy\",\"definition\":\"Continuing a path solely because of past unrecoverable investment.\"}],\"correct_option_key\":\"catastrophizing\",\"primary_trap\":\"Catastrophizing\",\"secondary_traps\":[\"Emotional Reasoning\",\"Confirmation Bias\",\"Fortune Telling\"],\"secondary_trap_keys\":[\"emotional_reasoning\",\"confirmation_bias\",\"fortune_telling\"],\"explanation_reveal\":\"after_commit\",\"explanation\":\"Primary Thinking Trap: Catastrophizing\\nManagement may assume that the complaint will destroy the company\'s reputation and respond defensively or impulsively.\\nSecondary Thinking Traps:\\nEmotional Reasoning: Responding out of embarrassment or anger.\\nConfirmation Bias: Selecting information that supports the company\'s preferred narrative.\\nFortune Telling: Assuming the complaint will either disappear or permanently damage the business.\"},{\"step_number\":3,\"key\":\"reality_check\",\"prompt\":\"Answer these questions before deciding what the situation means:\\n• What evidence should be gathered before issuing a detailed public response?\\n• Which operational failures could affect customers beyond the person who raised the complaint?\",\"tip\":\"Missing information is not evidence. Identify what you would need to know before becoming more certain.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What evidence should be gathered before issuing a detailed public response?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. Which operational failures could affect customers beyond the person who raised the complaint?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Service delivery records.\",\"Customer complaint history.\",\"Internal escalation records.\",\"Contractual service-level commitments.\",\"Communication with the customer.\",\"Corrective action records.\",\"Similar complaints from other customers.\",\"Actual financial and operational impact.\",\"The issue should be evaluated as both a customer relationship problem and a potential systemic failure.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Service delivery records.\",\"Customer complaint history.\",\"Internal escalation records.\",\"Contractual service-level commitments.\",\"Communication with the customer.\",\"Corrective action records.\",\"Similar complaints from other customers.\",\"Actual financial and operational impact.\",\"The issue should be evaluated as both a customer relationship problem and a potential systemic failure.\"]},{\"step_number\":4,\"key\":\"reframe\",\"prompt\":\"Explore other explanations and alternatives:\\n• What alternatives exist beyond publicly denying the allegations or admitting everything immediately?\\n• How could you acknowledge the concern while avoiding unsupported statements?\",\"insight\":\"Reframing does not mean forcing a positive interpretation. It means expanding the set of explanations or options before deciding.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"q1\",\"prompt\":\"1. What alternatives exist beyond publicly denying the allegations or admitting everything immediately?\"},{\"field_key\":\"q2\",\"prompt\":\"2. How could you acknowledge the concern while avoiding unsupported statements?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"Issue a brief acknowledgement of the concern.\",\"Contact the customer directly.\",\"Conduct an independent internal review.\",\"Correct verified service failures.\",\"Provide a factual update when findings are available.\",\"Strengthen customer grievance processes.\",\"Communicate directly with other affected customers where appropriate.\",\"Acknowledging a complaint does not require accepting every allegation as established fact.\"],\"reference_example\":[\"Issue a brief acknowledgement of the concern.\",\"Contact the customer directly.\",\"Conduct an independent internal review.\",\"Correct verified service failures.\",\"Provide a factual update when findings are available.\",\"Strengthen customer grievance processes.\",\"Communicate directly with other affected customers where appropriate.\",\"Acknowledging a complaint does not require accepting every allegation as established fact.\"]},{\"step_number\":5,\"key\":\"intervention\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do in the first 24–48 hours, and who would be responsible for each action?\",\"reminder\":\"There isn\'t always a perfect action. There is usually a reasonable next action based on the evidence available.\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"action\",\"prompt\":\"What would you do in the first 24–48 hours, and who would be responsible for each action?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":[\"A responsible approach would include:\",\"Appointing a crisis-response lead.\",\"Preserving relevant records.\",\"Contacting the customer.\",\"Verifying the allegations.\",\"Identifying immediate service risks.\",\"Preparing a factual communication.\",\"Implementing corrective actions.\",\"Monitoring customer confidence.\",\"The CEO should not delegate the entire crisis to the communications team. Operational accountability must remain with management.\"],\"reference_example\":\"A responsible approach would include:\\nAppointing a crisis-response lead.\\nPreserving relevant records.\\nContacting the customer.\\nVerifying the allegations.\\nIdentifying immediate service risks.\\nPreparing a factual communication.\\nImplementing corrective actions.\\nMonitoring customer confidence.\\nThe CEO should not delegate the entire crisis to the communications team. Operational accountability must remain with management.\"},{\"step_number\":6,\"key\":\"internalize\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\",\"inputs\":[{\"field_key\":\"principle\",\"prompt\":\"What judgment principle will you take away from this situation?\"}],\"thinkclear_thinking\":\"Reputation is built through consistent performance and credible responses when things go wrong. Managing appearances cannot substitute for correcting the underlying problem.\",\"reference_example\":\"Reputation is built through consistent performance and credible responses when things go wrong. Managing appearances cannot substitute for correcting the underlying problem.\"}],\"closing_reflection\":{\"prompt\":\"If your organisation spends more time defending its reputation than correcting the failures that damage it, what is it actually protecting?\",\"journal_input\":{\"field_key\":\"journal\",\"prompt\":\"Optional reflection entry — take a moment to reflect on today\'s scenario.\",\"required\":false}}}', '2026-11-10 12:00:00', '2026-11-10 12:00:00')
